 routing, by the one or more processors, the envelope back to the mail item digitization process; and 
 routing, by the one or more processors, an electronic image of a part of the mail item to a destination corresponding to the part; 

 wherein:
 the routing further comprises flagging, by the one or more processors, the electronic image as exceptional based on the printed message. 




       10. The media of  claim 9  wherein the method further comprises:
 receiving, by the one or more processors, the different address; 
 applying, by the labeler, to the envelope a mailing label including the different address; and 
 routing, by the one or more processors, the envelope from the holding bin to a mail delivery service. 



       11. The media of  claim 9  wherein in the method the routing comprises:
 applying, by the one or more processors, an electronic classification network to an input vector that includes:
 a physical parameter vector based on output from an optical probe of the envelope; 
 a string vector that includes a text string vector from the first mail item part; and 

