claims:
What is claimed is: 

       1. A method for forming of pre-preg structural members comprising the steps of:
 providing a mandrel having a plurality of forming blocks in segments, said forming blocks sized to receive a draped composite laminate assembly; 
 draping the composite laminate assembly on the mandrel maintaining all portions of the composite laminate assembly spaced from at least one shaping surface on each block during draping; 
 providing a saddle with at least one spline plate; 
 mounting the mandrel on the saddle; 
 maintaining the draped composite laminate assembly in contact with the forming blocks; and, 
 relaxing the shaping surfaces of the forming blocks onto the at least one spline plate, the forming blocks conforming to a curvature of the at least one spline plate to maintain the composite laminate assembly in tension. 



       2. The method defined in  claim 1  further comprising the step of providing a second spline plate as a portion of the saddle with a second center of curvature and said step of relaxing the mandrel form blocks includes relaxing second shaping surfaces of the forming blocks onto the second spline plate. 


       3. The method defined in  claim 1  wherein the step of providing a mandrel includes tensioning a cable in the forming blocks to draw the forming blocks together in a first tensioned position and the step of relaxing the mandrel comprises releasing the tension on the cable. 


       4. The method defined in  claim 2  further comprising restraining the forming blocks at a neutral axis prior to draping the composite laminate assembly on the mandrel. 


       5. The method defined in  claim 4  wherein the neutral axis is offset to maintain the draped composite laminate assembly in tension. 


       6. The method as defined in  claim 1  wherein the step of maintaining the draped composite laminate assembly in contact with the forming blocks comprises:
 providing a vacuum bag surrounding the composite laminate assembly; and 
 drawing vacuum on the vacuum bag to form the composite laminate assembly around the forming blocks. 



       7. A method for multiple axis forming of pre-preg structural members comprising the steps of:
 providing a mandrel having a plurality of forming blocks in segments, said forming blocks sized to receive a draped composite laminate assembly; 
 restraining the forming blocks at a neutral axis; 
 tensioning a cable in the forming blocks to draw the forming blocks together in a first tensioned position; 
 draping a composite laminate assembly on the mandrel maintaining all portions of the composite laminate assembly spaced from a first shaping surface and a second shaping surface on each block during draping; 
 providing a vacuum bag surrounding the composite laminate assembly; 
 drawing vacuum on the vacuum bag to form the composite laminate assembly around the forming blocks; 
 providing a saddle with a first spline plate and a second spline plate: 
 mounting the mandrel on the saddle; 
 maintaining the draped composite laminate assembly in contact with the forming blocks; and, 
 releasing the tension on the cable and relaxing the first shaping surface of each of the forming blocks onto the first spline plate and the second shaping surface of each of the forming blocks onto the second spline plate, the forming blocks conforming to a curvature of the first spline plate and conforming to a curvature of the second spline plate to maintain the composite laminate assembly in tension.

