claims:
What is claimed is: 

       1. A method of providing a container comprising:
 providing a metal cylindrical sidewall and a metal can end double-seamed to the sidewall, the sidewall having an interior surface and an exterior surface and extending from a first open end to a second end closed by the can end, the can end having an interior surface, the sidewall and the can end defining an interior of the container; 
 providing a liner sheet proximate the first end of the sidewall, the liner sheet having a first surface and a second surface opposite the first surface; 
 displacing the liner sheet toward the can end into the interior of the container; 
 displacing air from between the can end and the liner sheet; and 
 displacing air from between the sidewall and the liner sheet outside of the container and applying the first surface of the liner sheet to the interior surface of the sidewall. 



       2. The method of  claim 1 , wherein the liner sheet does not include BPA. 


       3. A method of providing a container comprising:
 providing a metal cylindrical sidewall and a metal can end double-seamed to the sidewall, the sidewall having an interior surface and an exterior surface and extending from a first open end to a second end closed by the can end, the can end having an interior surface, the sidewall and the can end defining an interior of the container; 
 providing a liner sheet proximate the first end of the sidewall, the liner sheet having a first surface and a second surface opposite the first surface; 
 heating the container; 
 applying adhesive to one of the first surface of the liner sheet and the sidewall of the container; 
 displacing the liner sheet toward the can end into the interior of the container; 
 displacing air from between the can end and the liner sheet; 
 displacing air from between the sidewall and the liner sheet outside of the container and applying the first surface of the liner sheet to the interior surface of the sidewall; and 
 applying the liner sheet to the sidewall and can end such that the liner sheet covers the interior surface of the can end and the interior surface of the sidewall. 



       4. A method of providing a container comprising:
 providing a metal cylindrical sidewall and a metal can end double-seamed to the sidewall, the sidewall having an interior surface and an exterior surface and extending from a first open end to a second end closed by the can end, the can end having an interior surface, the sidewall and the can end defining an interior of the container; 
 providing a liner sheet proximate the first end of the sidewall, the liner sheet having a first surface and a second surface opposite the first surface; 
 displacing the liner sheet toward the can end into the interior of the container; 
 displacing air from between the can end and the liner sheet; and 
 displacing air from between the sidewall and the liner sheet outside of the container and applying the first surface of the liner sheet to the interior surface of the sidewall; 
 wherein the step of displacing air between the can end and the liner and between the sidewall and the liner outside of the container and applying the first surface of the liner sheet to the can end and the sidewall includes providing a bladder; 
 displacing the bladder into the interior of the container; 
 inflating the bladder; 
 deflating the bladder; and 
 and removing the bladder from the interior of the container. 



       5. A method of providing a container comprising:
 providing a metal container including a sidewall having an interior surface, the sidewall extending from a first open end to a second end and an can end having an interior surface, the can end coupled to the sidewall closing the second end of the sidewall, the sidewall and the can end forming an open-topped enclosure; 
 providing a BPA-free film; 
 displacing the BPA-free film from the first open end of the sidewall to the can end in the interior of the open-topped enclosure; 
 removing air between the BPA-free film and the sidewall; and 
 adhering the BPA-free film to interior surfaces of the sidewall and the can end such that the film is substantially continuously applied to the interior surfaces of enclosure, the sidewall and the can end. 



       6. A method of providing a container comprising:
 providing a metal container including a sidewall having an interior surface, the sidewall extending from a first open end to a second end and a can end having an interior surface, the can end coupled to the sidewall closing the second end of the sidewall, the sidewall and the can end forming an open-topped enclosure; 
 providing a BPA-free film; 
 heating the metal container; and 
 adhering the BPA-free film to interior surfaces of the sidewall and the can end such that the film is substantially continuously applied to the interior surfaces of the sidewall and the can end. 



       7. The method of  claim 6 , further comprising providing adhesive on the interior surface of the sidewall and the interior surface of the can end. 


       8. The method of  claim 6 , further comprising providing adhesive on the BPA-free film. 


       9. The method of  claim 6 , further comprising
 providing a bladder;
 displacing the bladder and the BPA-free film into the open-topped enclosure; and 
 inflating the bladder thereby displacing the BPA-free film toward the sidewall. 




       10. The method of  claim 9 , further comprising deflating the bladder; and
 removing the bladder from the interior of the open-topped enclosure. 



       11. The method of  claim 6 , wherein the sidewall has a non-uniform diameter along a vertical axis of the sidewall. 


       12. The method of  claim 6 , further comprising removing a portion of the BPA-free film extending beyond the sidewall proximate the first open end. 


       13. The method of  claim 6 , further comprising adhering the BPA-free film prior to heating the container; and
 after adhering the BPA-free film to the sidewall and can end, allowing the container to cool. 



       14. A method of providing a container comprising:
 providing a metal container including a sidewall having an interior surface, the sidewall extending from a first open end to a second end and a can end having an interior surface, the can end coupled to the sidewall closing the second end of the sidewall, the sidewall and the can end forming an open-topped enclosure; 
 providing a BPA-free film; 
 providing a displaceable member; 
 displacing the member into the interior of the container; 
 withdrawing the member from a first location proximate the can end to a second location proximate the first open end of the sidewall and thereby removing air from between the BPA-free film and the side wall; and 
 adhering the BPA-free film to interior surfaces of the sidewall and the can end such that the film is substantially continuously applied to the interior surfaces of the sidewall and the can end. 



       15. An apparatus for applying a lining into a metal container, the metal container including a sidewall double-seamed to a can end, the container having a first open end and a second closed end, the apparatus comprising:
 a film mechanism configured to provide a film having a first side and a second side opposite the first side; and 
 a film displacement mechanism on the opposite side of the film as the metal container, the film displacement mechanism displaceable from a location outside the metal container through the first open end to a location inside the metal container proximate the can end thereby displacing the film into the container, the displacement mechanism being further displaceable from the location proximate the can end to a location outside of the container and configured to displace air from between the film and the sidewall such that the film is coupled to the sidewall; 
