A method of wireless communication, comprising:
at a relay apparatus associated with one or more other devices, receiving a first message from a downstream relay, wherein the first message includes an indication of a number of devices that are associated with the downstream relay; 
generating a second message for an upstream relay in response to the first message, wherein the second message is a request for an available capacity of the upstream relay; 
transmitting the second message to the upstream relay; 
receiving a response message from the upstream relay, the response message indicating the available capacity of the upstream relay; and 
determining whether the relay apparatus can serve the downstream relay based on the available capacity of the upstream relay.

