     25. A method of controlling an optical disc apparatus comprising the steps of:
 (A) acquiring a plurality of focus drive signals which are obtained by irradiating a light beam a data side of an information recording medium at a plurality of detection positions different with each other in a radial direction of the information recording medium, under the condition that a focus control is conducted such that the light beam irradiating the data side is in a predetermined converging state; 
 (B) determining at least one calculation expression used for calculating a shape of said data side based on the acquired focus drive signals; 
