Here is an example of a patent claim 1 for the invention title 'Method of manufacturing high voltage mixed-mode device', formatted as requested:

A method of manufacturing a high voltage mixed-mode device, the method comprising:
providing a semiconductor substrate;
forming a plurality of low voltage (LV) active regions and a plurality of high voltage (HV) active regions on the semiconductor substrate;
selectively forming a first gate dielectric layer having a first thickness over the LV active regions;
selectively forming a second gate dielectric layer having a second thickness, greater than the first thickness, over the HV active regions;
forming gate electrodes over the first and second gate dielectric layers;
forming LV source/drain regions within the LV active regions, the LV source/drain regions having a first junction depth and a first doping concentration profile;
forming HV source/drain regions within the HV active regions, the HV source/drain regions having a second junction depth and a second doping concentration profile, wherein the second junction depth is greater than the first junction depth and the second doping concentration profile includes a drift region configured for high voltage operation;
forming isolation structures between at least some of the LV active regions and the HV active regions; and
forming conductive interconnects electrically coupled to the LV source/drain regions, the HV source/drain regions, and the gate electrodes, thereby forming the high voltage mixed-mode device.

A method for updating an operation file without interrupting online processing, the method comprising:
