   a fault detection module coupled to said primary signal path, said fault detection module configured to detect a fault condition within said primary signal path;
   a switching module coupled to an output of said primary signal path and an output of said backup signal path, said switching module configured to select one of said primary signal path and said backup signal path as an active signal source;
   an output configured to provide an outgoing telecommunications signal from said active signal source; and
   a control module coupled to said fault detection module and said switching module, said control module configured to, upon detection of said fault condition by said fault detection module, command said switching module to switch from said primary signal path as the active signal source to said backup signal path as the active signal source;
   wherein said system is configured to perform said switch in a manner that ensures said outgoing telecommunications signal remains substantially hitless and substantially errorless throughout a transition period and after said transition period.

