A method for clock domain conflict analysis for timing graphs, comprising:
receiving a timing graph representing an integrated circuit design;
identifying a plurality of clock domains within the timing graph, each clock domain being associated with at least one clock signal;
identifying at least one clock domain crossing (CDC) within the timing graph, wherein the at least one CDC represents a data path or signal transition from a first clock domain to a second clock domain, the second clock domain being different from the first clock domain;
performing a clock domain conflict analysis on the at least one identified CDC to detect at least one potential timing conflict associated with the clock domain crossing; and
generating an output indicating the at least one detected potential timing conflict.

