A method for reducing irrelevant findings in vulnerability scan results; comprising:
receiving, by a computing system, raw vulnerability scan results generated by at least one vulnerability scanning tool, said raw vulnerability scan results identifying potential vulnerabilities in a plurality of target assets;
obtaining, by the computing system, contextual information associated with the plurality of target assets, wherein the contextual information comprises actual configuration data, operational environment data, or network topology data of the target assets;
correlating, by the computing system, the raw vulnerability scan results with the obtained contextual information to identify irrelevant findings or false positives within the raw vulnerability scan results, wherein an irrelevant finding or false positive is identified when a reported potential vulnerability does not correspond to an actual configuration or operational state of a respective target asset;
generating, by the computing system, refined vulnerability scan results by filtering out the identified irrelevant findings or false positives from the raw vulnerability scan results; and
providing, by the computing system, the refined vulnerability scan results for display, storage, or further automated remediation.

