a control unit communicatively coupled to at least one of said transmitter and said receiver, said control unit configured to dynamically adjust at least one operational parameter of said wireless energy transfer based on said determined separation distance, thereby optimizing energy transfer efficiency across a range of variable distances.

A wireless communication system employing frequency division multiple access, comprising:
a plurality of input interfaces configured to receive respective data streams;
a plurality of modulators, each coupled to a respective input interface and configured to modulate its received data stream onto a distinct carrier frequency;
a signal combiner coupled to the plurality of modulators and configured to combine said modulated signals into a composite signal;
a transmitter coupled to the signal combiner and configured to wirelessly transmit the composite signal;
a receiver configured to wirelessly receive the composite signal;
a plurality of filters, each coupled to the receiver and configured to isolate a distinct frequency band corresponding to one of the distinct carrier frequencies from the received composite signal;
a plurality of demodulators, each coupled to a respective filter and configured to demodulate a data stream from its respective isolated frequency band;
a plurality of output interfaces configured to output said demodulated data streams; and
a controller configured to assign said distinct carrier frequencies to the plurality of modulators and to coordinate the isolation of corresponding said distinct frequency bands by the plurality of filters.

A system for prosthesis delivery and implantation, comprising:
