A compound comprising a saturated aza-bicyclic ring system;
said ring system being substituted by at least one ether group of formula -O-R1;
wherein R1 is selected from the group consisting of optionally substituted C1-C10 alkyl, C3-C8 cycloalkyl, C6-C10 aryl, and 5- to 10-membered heteroaryl;
and wherein the saturated aza-bicyclic ring system is optionally substituted with one or more further substituents independently selected from the group consisting of halogen, cyano, nitro, C1-C6 alkyl, C1-C6 alkoxy, C1-C6 haloalkyl, and C1-C6 haloalkoxy;
or a pharmaceutically acceptable salt thereof.

A wireless transceiver, comprising:
a transmitter configured to generate and output a radio frequency (RF) transmit signal;
an antenna coupled to the transmitter and configured to transmit the RF transmit signal;
a receiver coupled to the antenna and configured to receive an RF composite signal therefrom, the RF composite signal including a desired external signal and a self-interference signal, wherein the self-interference signal originates from the RF transmit signal;
and an interference cancellation circuit coupled to the transmitter and the receiver, the interference cancellation circuit configured to:
    obtain a characteristic of the RF transmit signal;
    generate an interference replica signal based on the obtained characteristic, the interference replica signal modeling the self-interference signal;
    and subtractively combine the interference replica signal with the RF composite signal to produce a cancelled RF signal, wherein the self-interference signal is substantially reduced in the cancelled RF signal.

A method for initiating memory wear leveling, the method comprising:
monitoring write operations to a plurality of memory blocks within a non-volatile memory;
determining a wear status for each of the plurality of memory blocks based at least in part on the monitored write operations;
identifying a wear imbalance among the plurality of memory blocks based at least in part on the determined wear statuses;
generating a wear leveling initiation signal in response to identifying the wear imbalance; and
commencing a wear leveling process in the non-volatile memory based on the wear leveling initiation signal, wherein the wear leveling process redistributes data among the plurality of memory blocks to reduce the wear imbalance.

A method for determining absolute position of a tip of an elongate object on a plane surface with invariant features, comprising:
providing a plane surface having a plurality of invariant features at known absolute positions thereon;
obtaining sensor data representative of at least a subset of the plurality of invariant features;
obtaining sensor data representative of the tip of the elongate object;
determining a relative position of the tip of the elongate object with respect to the at least a subset of the plurality of invariant features based on the obtained sensor data; and
calculating the absolute position of the tip of the elongate object on the plane surface based on the determined relative position and the known absolute positions of the at least a subset of the plurality of invariant features.

A system for starting an aircraft engine, the system comprising:
a starter mechanism configured to impart rotational energy to rotating components of the aircraft engine;
a fuel delivery system configured to supply fuel to a combustion chamber of the aircraft engine;
an ignition system configured to generate an ignition spark within the combustion chamber;
a plurality of sensors configured to measure operating parameters of the aircraft engine, said operating parameters including at least engine rotational speed and engine temperature; and
an engine control unit communicatively coupled to the starter mechanism, the fuel delivery system, the ignition system, and the plurality of sensors, wherein the engine control unit is configured to execute an engine start sequence comprising:
initiating activation of the starter mechanism to accelerate the rotating components of the aircraft engine;
commanding the fuel delivery system to introduce fuel into the combustion chamber upon reaching a first predetermined rotational speed;
activating the ignition system to generate the ignition spark upon or after introduction of fuel into the combustion chamber;
monitoring the operating parameters from the plurality of sensors to determine when the aircraft engine achieves a self-sustaining operational state; and
deactivating the starter mechanism and the ignition system upon confirmation of the self-sustaining operational state.

A system for dispensing medical products, the system comprising:
