characterizing group delay associated with each of the plurality of transmit paths;
calculating a compensation for group delay disparities among the plurality of transmit paths, based on said characterized group delay; and
applying said compensation to at least one of the plurality of beamforming signals to equalize group delays across the plurality of transmit paths.

1. An apparatus for filtering water from a fluid stream originating from an oil and gas well, the apparatus comprising:
