A speech recognition system, comprising:
an audio input module configured to receive speech audio signals;
a feature extraction module coupled to the audio input module, configured to process said speech audio signals into a sequence of acoustic features;
an acoustic model coupled to the feature extraction module, configured to generate acoustic likelihoods for sub-word units based on said sequence of acoustic features;
a vocabulary database comprising a plurality of words exceeding a threshold size characteristic of conventional speech recognition systems, wherein said vocabulary database is structured for efficient access and retrieval of individual words and sub-word units thereof;
a language model, coupled to said vocabulary database, configured to predict sequences of words from said vocabulary database, wherein said language model employs a hierarchical or statistical compression scheme to manage said plurality of words efficiently;
a decoder, coupled to said acoustic model, said language model, and said vocabulary database, configured to generate a sequence of recognized words based on said acoustic likelihoods and said language model, wherein said decoder utilizes a multi-pass search strategy with dynamic pruning to effectively navigate a search space defined by said huge vocabulary database; and
an output module coupled to said decoder, configured to provide said sequence of recognized words.

