1. A method for determining the status of and detecting a pancreatic B-cell associated autoimmune disease in a subject, comprising:
    obtaining a biological sample from the subject;
    detecting in the biological sample the presence or level of at least one biomarker indicative of pancreatic B-cell autoimmunity;
    comparing the detected presence or level of the at least one biomarker to a predetermined reference value; and
    determining, based on the comparison, the status of a pancreatic B-cell associated autoimmune disease in the subject.

A memory array, comprising:
    a semiconductor substrate;
    a plurality of memory cells formed over the semiconductor substrate;
    an isolation region formed within the semiconductor substrate; and
    a digit line electrically coupled to at least one of the plurality of memory cells, wherein the digit line is buried within the isolation region;

A flow measuring apparatus, comprising:
a conduit defining a fluid flow path;
a constriction element disposed within the fluid flow path, said constriction element defining a narrowed cross-sectional area through which fluid flows;
a deflectable membrane operatively coupled to the constriction element such that the deflectable membrane is exposed to a pressure differential generated across the constriction element by fluid flow;
and a sensing element configured to detect deflection of the deflectable membrane and to generate a signal indicative of a flow rate through the fluid flow path based on the detected deflection.

A standard interface rack, comprising:
a frame structure defining a plurality of standardized mounting bays;
a power distribution system integrated within the frame structure, the power distribution system including a plurality of standardized power connectors disposed within each of the plurality of standardized mounting bays, wherein the standardized power connectors are configured to deliver electrical power to electronic modules insertable into the mounting bays;
a data communication system integrated within the frame structure, the data communication system including a plurality of standardized data connectors disposed within each of the plurality of standardized mounting bays, wherein the standardized data connectors are configured to enable data communication between electronic modules insertable into the mounting bays and with external systems; and
wherein each of the plurality of standardized mounting bays is configured to mechanically and electrically receive distinct electronic modules conforming to a predefined interoperability standard, thereby facilitating interchangeability and interoperability among the distinct electronic modules.

A method for computing the relative likelihood of failures, the method comprising:
identifying a plurality of potential failure events associated with a system or process;
obtaining data indicative of failure conditions or characteristics for each of the plurality of potential failure events;
computing, for each identified potential failure event, an individual likelihood score based on the obtained data;
comparing the individual likelihood scores of the plurality of potential failure events to determine a relative likelihood for each identified potential failure event; and
generating an output indicative of the determined relative likelihoods.

1. A system for haptic confirmation of commands, the system comprising:
    an input interface configured to receive a user command;
    a processor communicatively coupled to the input interface, the processor configured to:
        process the received user command; and
        determine a haptic feedback profile associated with the user command;
    a haptic feedback generator communicatively coupled to the processor, the haptic feedback generator configured to generate a haptic sensation according to the determined haptic feedback profile;
    wherein the generated haptic sensation provides a haptic confirmation of the user command to the user.

A high-voltage NMOS transistor, comprising:
a semiconductor substrate of a first conductivity type;
a gate electrode disposed over the semiconductor substrate;
a gate dielectric layer positioned between the gate electrode and the semiconductor substrate, the gate dielectric layer having a thickness configured to withstand breakdown voltages greater than a predetermined low-voltage threshold;
a source region of a second conductivity type formed in the semiconductor substrate, laterally adjacent to a first side of the gate electrode;
a drain region of the second conductivity type formed in the semiconductor substrate, laterally separated from a second side of the gate electrode; and
an extended drain drift region of the second conductivity type, more lightly doped than the drain region, disposed in the semiconductor substrate between a channel region beneath the gate electrode and the drain region, said extended drain drift region configured to sustain high drain-to-source voltages.

A method for forming a metal oxide film, comprising:
  providing a substrate within a reaction chamber;
  introducing a metal-containing precursor into the reaction chamber;
  introducing an oxygen-containing precursor into the reaction chamber;
  maintaining the substrate at a temperature suitable for forming the metal oxide film; and
  reacting the metal-containing precursor and the oxygen-containing precursor on a surface of the substrate to form the metal oxide film.

A method for estimating the position of a sound source for online calibration of auditory cue to location transformations, the method comprising:
receiving a plurality of sound signals generated by a sound source, wherein each sound signal of the plurality is received by a respective sensor at a different location;
extracting at least one auditory cue from the received sound signals, the at least one auditory cue representative of a spatial characteristic of the sound source;
estimating an initial position of the sound source based on the at least one auditory cue and a current set of auditory cue to location transformations;
determining a difference between the estimated initial position and a reference position of the sound source, wherein the reference position is independently determined or known; and
updating the current set of auditory cue to location transformations based on the determined difference, thereby performing online calibration of the auditory cue to location transformations.

A programmable controller, comprising:
a processor configured to execute program instructions and process data;
a memory coupled to the processor, the memory storing the program instructions and data;
an input interface coupled to the processor, the input interface configured to receive input signals from one or more external devices;
an output interface coupled to the processor, the output interface configured to generate output control signals for one or more external devices; and
wherein the processor is configured to execute the stored program instructions based on the received input signals and the stored data to generate the output control signals for controlling an operation of the one or more external devices.

An information reproducing method, comprising:
receiving a data stream comprising encoded information;
analyzing the received data stream to identify at least one encoding characteristic of the encoded information;
selecting a decoding scheme from a plurality of available decoding schemes based on the identified encoding characteristic;
processing the encoded information using the selected decoding scheme to generate decoded information; and
outputting the decoded information in a perceptible form.

A computing system comprising:
a volatile memory configured to store active data;
a non-volatile flash memory configured to store persistent data;
a control unit communicatively coupled to the volatile memory and the non-volatile flash memory;
wherein the control unit is configured to:
detect a trigger event indicating an impending change in power state or an operating condition affecting data retention in the volatile memory;
in response to detecting the trigger event, initiate a back-up operation to automatically transfer the active data from the volatile memory to the non-volatile flash memory for persistent storage;
subsequently detect a recovery event indicating a return to an operational state; and
in response to detecting the recovery event, initiate a restoration operation to automatically transfer the persistent data from the non-volatile flash memory to the volatile memory;
thereby enabling seamless preservation and retrieval of the active data across the power state change or operating condition.

A method for producing and processing a material slab, comprising the steps of:
forming a raw material into an elongated slab;
continuously conveying the elongated slab from a forming station to a processing station;
performing at least one processing operation on the elongated slab at the processing station, wherein the at least one processing operation is selected from the group consisting of cutting, shaping, and surface treating the elongated slab; and
collecting discrete slab portions after said performing at least one processing operation;

A method of charging a battery, the method comprising:
supplying a charging current or voltage to the battery;
monitoring at least one operating parameter of the battery, wherein the at least one operating parameter includes at least one of battery voltage, battery current, battery temperature, or battery state of charge;
dynamically adjusting at least one charging parameter of the supplied charging current or voltage based on the monitored operating parameter;
wherein the dynamic adjustment is performed to optimize at least one of charging speed, battery lifespan, or safety of the battery.

1. An organic light emitting device, comprising:
   a substrate;
   an anode disposed over the substrate;
   a cathode disposed over the anode; and
   an organic layer stack disposed between the anode and the cathode, the organic layer stack comprising at least one hole transport layer, an organic light emitting layer, and at least one electron transport layer;
   wherein the organic light emitting device is configured to emit light upon application of an electrical current between the anode and the cathode.

1. A method for making chip size semiconductor packages, the method comprising:
    providing a plurality of semiconductor dice;
    providing a substrate panel comprising a plurality of package sites;
    attaching each of the plurality of semiconductor dice to a respective one of the plurality of package sites on the substrate panel in a flip-chip configuration;
    dispensing an underfill material between each of the plurality of semiconductor dice and the substrate panel;
    curing the underfill material;
    forming an encapsulant over the plurality of semiconductor dice and portions of the substrate panel, wherein the encapsulant is molded such that it extends minimally beyond lateral edges of the respective semiconductor dice;
    forming a plurality of external electrical contacts on a bottom surface of the substrate panel, each plurality of external electrical contacts being electrically coupled to a respective one of the plurality of semiconductor dice, and each plurality of external electrical contacts being configured to be substantially co-extensive with a footprint of the respective one of the plurality of semiconductor dice; and
    singulating the substrate panel into a plurality of individual chip size semiconductor packages.

An immersion lithographic apparatus, comprising:
a projection system configured to project a patterned beam of radiation onto a substrate;
a substrate stage configured to hold the substrate;
an immersion liquid supply system configured to supply an immersion liquid into a space between the projection system and the substrate;
and a pressure sensor configured to measure pressure of the immersion liquid in the space between the projection system and the substrate.

A radiofrequency amplifier, comprising:
a radiofrequency input port configured to receive an input radiofrequency signal;
a radiofrequency output port configured to provide an amplified radiofrequency output signal;
an active amplifying component electrically coupled between the radiofrequency input port and the radiofrequency output port, the active amplifying component configured to amplify the input radiofrequency signal;
a biasing circuit configured to provide operating power to the active amplifying component;
an input impedance matching network coupled between the radiofrequency input port and an input of the active amplifying component, the input impedance matching network configured to match an impedance of the radiofrequency input port to an input impedance of the active amplifying component; and
an output impedance matching network coupled between an output of the active amplifying component and the radiofrequency output port, the output impedance matching network configured to match an output impedance of the active amplifying component to an impedance of the radiofrequency output port.

An apparatus, comprising:
a voltage generator;
the voltage generator configured to provide an adjustable voltage drop;
the adjustable voltage drop representing a voltage drop of at least one of a memory cell, a current mirror circuit, and a replica circuit.

1. An apparatus for providing cooling and heating utilizing waste heat, comprising:
    a waste heat source;
    a thermal energy extraction unit configured to transfer thermal energy from said waste heat source to a working fluid;
    a cooling subsystem operatively coupled to said thermal energy extraction unit and configured to provide a cooling effect;
    a heating subsystem operatively coupled to said thermal energy extraction unit and configured to provide a heating effect; and
    a control system configured to regulate the operation of said thermal energy extraction unit, said cooling subsystem, and said heating subsystem to selectively provide said cooling effect, said heating effect, or both, based on sensed operational parameters and a predetermined demand.

An electronic device comprising:
a processing unit configured to execute instructions;
a memory unit coupled to the processing unit and configured to store instructions and data;
a plurality of sensors configured to detect environmental conditions and/or user interaction associated with the electronic device;
a power management unit coupled to the processing unit and configured to control power delivery to various components of the electronic device;
wherein the processing unit is further configured to:
acquire historical usage data associated with the electronic device and sensor data from the plurality of sensors;
analyze the acquired historical usage data and sensor data to generate a prediction regarding future usage patterns or power demands of the electronic device;
generate a power management command based on the prediction; and
transmit the power management command to the power management unit, wherein the power management unit is further configured to adjust at least one operational parameter of the electronic device in response to the received power management command to optimize power consumption.

A system for magnetic fixturing of optical components on a bench for solder attach, the system comprising:
a bench platform;
a reconfigurable optical component fixture positionable on the bench platform;
at least one magnetic element integrated within or coupled to the reconfigurable optical component fixture; and
at least one optical component comprising a magnetically responsive feature configured to engage with the at least one magnetic element;
wherein the at least one magnetic element is configured to securely hold the at least one optical component in a predetermined orientation and position relative to the bench platform for a solder attachment process; and
further wherein the reconfigurable optical component fixture is configured to provide unimpeded access to a solderable interface of the at least one optical component during the solder attachment process.

A method for improved fabrication of a semiconductor device, the method comprising:
providing a semiconductor substrate having a region designated for device formation;
forming at least one stress-inducing structure in proximity to the region of the semiconductor substrate;
generating a localized stress field within the region of the semiconductor substrate via the at least one stress-inducing structure; and
modifying at least one material property, electrical property, or structural characteristic of the semiconductor substrate within said region by said localized stress field to enhance device performance or reliability.

A memory circuit comprising:
a field effect transistor (FET) configured as a memory cell, the FET having a gate, a source, and a drain;
wherein the FET is configured to store a data state by exhibiting a threshold voltage shift based on a stored charge;
a word line electrically coupled to the gate of the FET;
a bit line electrically coupled to at least one of the source and the drain of the FET; and
control circuitry configured to apply voltages to the word line and the bit line to program, read, or erase the data state stored in the FET.

An apparatus for timing recovery in a wireless transceiver, comprising:
a receiver configured to receive an incoming wireless signal;
a sampler configured to sample the incoming wireless signal to produce sampled data at a sampling rate determined by a sampling clock;
a timing error detector coupled to the sampler, the timing error detector configured to generate a timing error signal based on the sampled data, the timing error signal indicative of a timing misalignment between the sampling clock and a symbol timing of the incoming wireless signal;
a loop filter coupled to the timing error detector, the loop filter configured to filter the timing error signal to produce a filtered timing error signal; and
a clock recovery unit coupled to the loop filter, the clock recovery unit configured to adjust the sampling clock based on the filtered timing error signal to synchronize the sampling clock with the symbol timing of the incoming wireless signal.

A pluggable drive carrier assembly comprising:
a carrier housing configured to receive and secure a data storage drive therein;
an electrical connector disposed on a rear portion of the carrier housing, the electrical connector configured to electrically couple with a mating connector on a backplane when the carrier housing is inserted into a drive bay;
a retention mechanism coupled to the carrier housing, the retention mechanism configured to selectively secure the carrier housing within the drive bay and allow for tool-less removal of the carrier housing therefrom; and
at least one guide feature disposed on an exterior surface of the carrier housing, the at least one guide feature configured to engage with a corresponding guide feature within the drive bay to facilitate alignment during insertion and removal of the carrier housing.

An apparatus for generating an ultra small spot, comprising:
a source configured to generate an energy beam;
a focusing assembly operably coupled to said source and configured to receive said energy beam, said focusing assembly comprising at least one high numerical aperture element and structured to converge said energy beam onto a target plane;
wherein said focusing assembly is further configured to form a spot at said target plane having a characteristic dimension substantially less than a diffraction limit of said energy beam; and
a control system operably coupled to at least one of said source and said focusing assembly to regulate emission and focusing of said energy beam.

A method for manufacturing a storage tank for gas and liquid, comprising:
forming a main body portion of the tank from a sheet material;
forming at least one end closure for the tank from a sheet material;
joining the at least one end closure to the main body portion along a seam to form a closed vessel;
sealing the seam to ensure leak-tightness of the closed vessel; and
pressurizing the closed vessel to a predetermined test pressure to verify its structural integrity and leak-tightness.

1. A method of fabricating a semiconductor device, comprising:
providing a substrate;
forming at least one semiconductor layer over the substrate;
forming at least one device structure within or on the at least one semiconductor layer; and
forming at least one interconnect structure electrically coupled to the at least one device structure.

A method for diagnosing chronic stress or a related disorder in a subject, comprising:
obtaining a biological sample from the subject;
determining a level of at least one biomarker associated with chronic stress or a related disorder in the biological sample;
comparing the determined level of the at least one biomarker to a predetermined reference level; and
diagnosing the subject as having chronic stress or a related disorder based on a deviation of the determined level from the predetermined reference level.

1. A method of forming semiconductor structures with contact holes, the method comprising:
    providing a semiconductor substrate;
    forming a dielectric layer over the semiconductor substrate;
    forming a patterned mask layer over the dielectric layer, wherein the patterned mask layer defines at least one opening corresponding to a desired contact hole location;
    etching the dielectric layer through the at least one opening in the patterned mask layer to form at least one contact hole, wherein the at least one contact hole extends through the dielectric layer to expose an underlying region of the semiconductor substrate or an underlying conductive layer;
    filling the at least one contact hole with a conductive material.

A Schottky diode comprising:
a semiconductor substrate of a first conductivity type having a first surface and a second surface opposite the first surface;
an ohmic contact disposed on the first surface of the semiconductor substrate;
a Schottky metal layer disposed on the second surface of the semiconductor substrate, said Schottky metal layer forming a rectifying contact with the semiconductor substrate;
a localized high-doping region of the first conductivity type formed in the semiconductor substrate immediately beneath and in contact with a central portion of the Schottky metal layer, said localized high-doping region configured to reduce an effective Schottky barrier height to thereby increase forward current of the Schottky diode;
and a field termination structure formed in the semiconductor substrate peripheral to the localized high-doping region and laterally surrounding the rectifying contact, said field termination structure configured to mitigate electric field crowding at an edge of the rectifying contact to thereby improve reverse bias characteristics of the Schottky diode.

A method for fabricating a power semiconductor device, comprising:
providing a semiconductor substrate;
forming a voltage sustaining layer on the semiconductor substrate;
forming a terraced trench within the voltage sustaining layer, the terraced trench having a plurality of laterally offset steps along at least one sidewall thereof, said steps defining a varying depth profile into the voltage sustaining layer;
filling the terraced trench with a dielectric material to form a trench isolation region; and
forming a plurality of floating islands in the voltage sustaining layer, wherein the plurality of floating islands are physically separated from each other by the trench isolation region.

A display control device comprising:
a display unit configured to render a graphical user interface (GUI);
an input unit configured to acquire user input data;
a processor coupled to the display unit and the input unit;
a memory coupled to the processor and storing program instructions;
wherein the processor, in response to executing the program instructions, is configured to:
generate a plurality of graphical elements forming the GUI for presentation on the display unit;
identify a state of the display control device or an environmental parameter; and
dynamically modify at least one visual attribute or interactive functionality of at least one of the plurality of graphical elements based on the identified state of the display control device or the environmental parameter.

A method for treating a substrate, comprising:
receiving a substrate to be treated;
determining one or more treatment parameters for the received substrate;
generating a sequence of machine-executable control instructions based on the one or more determined treatment parameters; and
operating a substrate treatment apparatus to apply a treatment to the substrate according to the generated sequence of machine-executable control instructions.

A rotation-angle-detecting apparatus, comprising:
    a rotatable member configured to rotate about an axis;
    a stationary member positioned relative to the rotatable member;
    a sensing arrangement configured to generate a signal indicative of a relative angular position between the rotatable member and the stationary member;
    a processing unit communicatively coupled to the sensing arrangement, the processing unit configured to determine the rotation angle of the rotatable member based on the generated signal; and
    an output interface configured to provide the determined rotation angle.

1. An imaging apparatus, comprising:
a light source configured to emit light towards a subject;
an optical system configured to receive light reflected or transmitted from the subject and form an image;
an image sensor configured to capture the image formed by the optical system and generate image data; and
a processor configured to receive the image data from the image sensor and generate an output image.

A coupling comprising:
a first coupling member defining a recessed receiving portion having an inner engagement surface;
a second coupling member defining an insertable male portion having an outer engagement surface, wherein said male portion is configured for matingly engaging said recessed receiving portion;
a plurality of radially movable locking elements circumferentially disposed within said first coupling member, each of said locking elements biased by a spring mechanism towards an extended position;
an annular groove defined on said outer engagement surface of said male portion, configured to receive said extended locking elements to secure said first coupling member to said second coupling member; and
an actuation collar slidably disposed on said first coupling member, said actuation collar configured to selectively retract said locking elements from said annular groove to permit disengagement of said male portion from said recessed receiving portion.

Here is an example of patent claim 1 for the invention title 'Methods and equipment for cutting food products', structured as a method claim:

A method for cutting food products, comprising:
    providing a food product to a cutting station;
    positioning the food product relative to at least one cutting element;
    actuating the at least one cutting element to engage and sever the food product along a predetermined cutting path;
    separating the severed portions of the food product from any remaining unsevered portions; and
    discharging the severed portions from the cutting station.

A jig for aligning a door hinge for mounting to a vehicle by an automatic mounting system, said jig comprising:
a main body;
a hinge reception portion integrated with the main body, said hinge reception portion configured to securely receive and hold the door hinge in a predetermined orientation;
at least one vehicle interface element extending from the main body, said at least one vehicle interface element configured to precisely engage a datum surface on the vehicle body to establish a fixed alignment of the jig relative to the vehicle; and
an automatic system interface portion integrated with the main body, said automatic system interface portion configured to mechanically couple with an end effector of the automatic system for manipulation and control of the jig;
wherein, when the door hinge is received in the hinge reception portion and the at least one vehicle interface element engages the datum surface on the vehicle body, the door hinge is held in a precise mounting position relative to the vehicle for subsequent attachment by the automatic system.

Here is a patent claim 1 for the given invention title, formatted as requested:

An apparatus for triggering a sliding and hinged sun roof, comprising:
a user input device configured to receive a user command for a sun roof panel, the user command indicating a desired movement selected from a sliding movement and a hinging movement;
a control unit electronically coupled to the user input device, the control unit configured to interpret the user command;
a sun roof assembly comprising the sun roof panel, a sliding rail system for enabling the sliding movement of the sun roof panel relative to a roof opening, and a hinge mechanism for enabling the hinging movement of the sun roof panel relative to the roof opening;
at least one actuator mechanically coupled to the sun roof assembly and electronically coupled to the control unit;
wherein the control unit is further configured to energize the at least one actuator to initiate the desired movement of the sun roof panel, such that the sun roof panel either performs the sliding movement along the sliding rail system or performs the hinging movement via the hinge mechanism, based on the interpreted user command.

A firearm trigger mechanism, comprising:
a housing configured to be mounted within a firearm frame;
a trigger pivotally mounted within the housing, the trigger having an engagement surface;
a sear pivotally mounted within the housing, the sear configured to engage a hammer or striker of the firearm, wherein the sear is operably coupled to the engagement surface of the trigger;
a trigger pull weight adjustment mechanism, including an adjustment screw threadably engaged with the housing and positioned to exert variable pressure on a spring biasing at least one of the trigger and the sear;
a trigger travel adjustment mechanism, including at least one adjustment screw threadably engaged with the housing and configured to limit a range of pivotal movement of the trigger;
wherein rotation of the adjustment screw of the trigger pull weight adjustment mechanism varies a force required to disengage the sear from the hammer or striker; and
wherein rotation of the at least one adjustment screw of the trigger travel adjustment mechanism varies a distance of travel of the trigger.

A method for extruding tire rubber material, the method comprising:
providing a pre-mixed, unvulcanized tire rubber compound at a predetermined temperature;
feeding the pre-mixed, unvulcanized tire rubber compound into an extruder apparatus having at least one screw for plasticizing and pressurizing the compound;
forcing the plasticized and pressurized tire rubber compound through a shaping die to form an extruded profile having a predetermined cross-sectional shape suitable for a tire component;
cooling the extruded profile while maintaining its predetermined cross-sectional shape; and
collecting the cooled extruded profile.

A method for dynamic flow-based multi-path load balancing with quality of service assurances, comprising:
  receiving network traffic comprising a plurality of data flows;
  identifying a plurality of available network paths for transmitting the network traffic;
  associating a quality of service (QoS) requirement with each of the plurality of data flows;
  dynamically monitoring performance characteristics of each of the plurality of available network paths, wherein the performance characteristics include at least current load and available bandwidth;
  dynamically selecting, for each data flow, a target network path from the plurality of available network paths by evaluating the associated QoS requirement of the respective data flow against the dynamically monitored performance characteristics of the plurality of available network paths, such that the selection provides the associated QoS assurance for the respective data flow while balancing network traffic load across the plurality of available network paths;
  directing each data flow along its respective target network path.

A system for location positioning using a machine-to-machine (M2M) ecosystem, comprising:
a target M2M device configured to be associated with an asset whose location is to be determined;
a plurality of anchor M2M devices distributed within a defined area, each anchor M2M device having a known or determinable geographical position;
an M2M communication network communicatively coupled to the target M2M device and the plurality of anchor M2M devices, wherein the target M2M device and the plurality of anchor M2M devices are configured to exchange location-related data over the M2M communication network; and
a location determination unit communicatively coupled to the M2M communication network, wherein the location determination unit is configured to receive the location-related data from the target M2M device and the plurality of anchor M2M devices, and further configured to calculate a current geographical location of the asset based on the received location-related data.

A semiconductor memory device, comprising:
a main memory array comprising a plurality of memory cells arranged in rows and columns;
a redundant memory array comprising a plurality of redundant memory cells;
a defect address storage circuit configured to store at least one address corresponding to a defective memory location within the main memory array;
an address input circuit configured to receive an input address for accessing a memory location; and
an address control circuit coupled to the address input circuit, the defect address storage circuit, the main memory array, and the redundant memory array, the address control circuit configured to compare the input address with the at least one stored defective address and, upon a match, select a memory location within the redundant memory array for access instead of the defective memory location within the main memory array, and upon no match, select a memory location within the main memory array for access.

A method for diagnosing electrical cables, comprising:
exposing an electrical cable to a penetrating energy beam;
acquiring projection data by detecting the penetrating energy beam after passing through the electrical cable, wherein the acquisition is performed from multiple angular positions around a longitudinal axis of the electrical cable;
generating a tomographic reconstruction of a cross-sectional image of the electrical cable based on the acquired projection data;
analyzing the tomographic reconstruction to identify a structural characteristic, degradation, or defect within the electrical cable; and
generating a diagnostic assessment of the electrical cable based on the identified structural characteristic, degradation, or defect.

A system for ship propulsion, the system comprising:
an airborne rigid kite body configured to generate aerodynamic lift and drag forces when exposed to an airflow;
an on-board power plant coupled to the rigid kite body, said power plant configured to generate power for operating at least one component of the airborne rigid kite body;
at least one active thrust generating mechanism coupled to the rigid kite body and powered by the on-board power plant, said active thrust generating mechanism configured to augment propulsion forces generated by the rigid kite body;
a tether having a first end coupled to the rigid kite body and a second end configured to be coupled to a ship, said tether configured to transmit propulsion forces from the rigid kite body to the ship; and
a control system configured to adjust flight parameters of the rigid kite body to optimize propulsion forces transmitted via the tether.

A computer-implemented method for an integrated system-of-systems modeling environment, the method comprising:
    providing a graphical user interface configured to facilitate user definition and configuration of a plurality of heterogeneous constituent systems, wherein each constituent system is independently operable and possesses distinct functionalities;
    receiving, via the graphical user interface, system definitions for each of the plurality of heterogeneous constituent systems;
    receiving, via the graphical user interface, interaction definitions specifying interdependencies, communication protocols, and interface specifications among the plurality of heterogeneous constituent systems;
    constructing a plurality of individual system models based on the received system definitions, wherein each individual system model represents the behavior of a respective constituent system;
    integrating the plurality of individual system models and the received interaction definitions into a unified system-of-systems (SoS) model, wherein the unified SoS model is configured to represent a combined operational behavior and emergent properties arising from the interactions of the plurality of heterogeneous constituent systems;
    executing the unified SoS model to simulate a dynamic behavior of the SoS under at least one defined scenario;
    analyzing simulation outputs from the executed unified SoS model to identify performance characteristics or emergent properties of the SoS that are not readily apparent from individual constituent system models; and
    presenting, via the graphical user interface, simulation results and analysis outputs related to the dynamic behavior, performance characteristics, or emergent properties of the SoS.

A system for a vehicle, comprising:
a display device disposed within the vehicle;
a plurality of input devices, wherein each input device is configured to receive user input from a distinct user within the vehicle;
a processor operatively coupled to the display device and the plurality of input devices; and
a memory operatively coupled to the processor and storing instructions that, when executed by the processor, cause the processor to:
display a graphical user interface on the display device;
display a plurality of cursors on the graphical user interface, wherein each cursor of the plurality of cursors is associated with a respective one of the plurality of input devices;
receive input from each of the plurality of input devices;
control a position and/or state of each respective cursor on the display device based on the input received from its associated input device; and
facilitate interaction with at least one vehicle function or at least one graphical element of the graphical user interface via at least one of the plurality of cursors.

A method for client-side scaling of web server farm architectures in a cloud data center, the method comprising:
acquiring, by a client device, server characteristic data for a plurality of web servers comprising a web server farm operating within a cloud data center, wherein the server characteristic data indicates an operational state or capacity of each of the plurality of web servers;
determining, by the client device, a web request distribution strategy among the plurality of web servers based on the acquired server characteristic data;
transmitting, by the client device, one or more web requests to at least one web server of the plurality of web servers according to the determined web request distribution strategy; and
periodically re-acquiring server characteristic data and re-determining the web request distribution strategy to dynamically adjust web request transmission based on changes in the operational state or capacity of the plurality of web servers.

A system for dynamically controlling the allocation of resources in a data processing system, the system comprising:
a resource monitoring module configured to obtain real-time usage data for a plurality of computing resources within the data processing system and to obtain demand data from a plurality of applications executing within the data processing system;
a resource analysis module coupled to the resource monitoring module, the resource analysis module configured to analyze the real-time usage data and the demand data to identify resource bottlenecks or underutilized resources, and to determine, based on said analysis, a modified allocation scheme for the plurality of computing resources; and
a resource allocation module coupled to the resource analysis module, the resource allocation module configured to apply the modified allocation scheme to control the allocation of the plurality of computing resources among the plurality of applications;
wherein the resource monitoring module, the resource analysis module, and the resource allocation module are configured to operate in a continuous feedback loop to adaptively adjust resource allocation based on changing usage and demand conditions.

An electrically conductive article, comprising:
an electrically conductive thermoplastic elastomer composition;
said composition comprising:
from about 50 wt% to about 99 wt% of at least one thermoplastic elastomer;
from about 1 wt% to about 50 wt% of at least one electrically conductive filler; and
optionally, one or more additives selected from the group consisting of plasticizers, stabilizers, processing aids, flame retardants, colorants, and mixtures thereof;
wherein said electrically conductive thermoplastic elastomer composition has an electrical volume resistivity of less than about 10^9 ohm-cm; and
wherein said article is formed from said electrically conductive thermoplastic elastomer composition.

A pump system comprising:
a main pump having a suction inlet and a discharge outlet, configured to pump a liquid;
a priming circuit fluidly connected to said main pump, said priming circuit comprising a priming pump and a priming valve, said priming pump configured to draw air from at least one of said suction inlet and a casing of said main pump;
a sensor configured to detect a priming condition of said main pump, said priming condition comprising at least one of a presence of liquid at said suction inlet and a vacuum level within said main pump casing; and
