receiving, at the TUT, an indication of successful joining of the trunk group;
initiating, by the TUT, a push-to-talk (PTT) communication session by transmitting a PTT request signal to the trunk service platform via the LTE network;
receiving, at the trunk service platform, the PTT request signal;
establishing, by the LTE network, a dedicated radio bearer for the PTT communication session between the TUT and the trunk service platform, wherein the dedicated radio bearer is configured with quality of service (QoS) parameters optimized for real-time voice communication;
transmitting voice data, by the TUT, over the established dedicated radio bearer to the trunk service platform; and
distributing, by the trunk service platform, the transmitted voice data to one or more other trunk user terminals within the trunk group via the LTE network.

