wherein the data output of each stage, except a last stage, is coupled to the data input of a subsequent stage;
a clock input configured to receive a primary clock signal;
a control signal generation circuit coupled to the clock input and configured to generate a plurality of distinct stage control signals based on the primary clock signal and at least one initial control input; and
wherein each stage of the plurality of serially connected stages is configured to update its data storage element with a data value from its data input and to transfer its stored data value to its data output in response to a corresponding one of the plurality of distinct stage control signals.

An antenna apparatus, comprising:
a monopole radiating element having a primary conductor extending from a feed point;
a ground plane electromagnetically coupled to said monopole radiating element;
a feed network coupled to said monopole radiating element and said ground plane;
wherein said monopole radiating element is structured to exhibit a plurality of distinct resonant frequencies, thereby enabling multi-band operation across a plurality of communication frequency bands; and
wherein said monopole radiating element is further structured to provide a first antenna function optimized for a first communication purpose and a second antenna function optimized for a second communication purpose, said second communication purpose distinct from said first communication purpose.

1. A method for printing letters using a line thermal head, the method comprising:
receiving input data representing characters to be printed;
generating a plurality of print data rows, each print data row corresponding to a scan line of a character image;
providing a print medium adjacent to a line thermal head, the line thermal head comprising a plurality of heating elements extending across a print width;
sequentially moving the print medium relative to the line thermal head;
for each of the plurality of print data rows, selectively activating a subset of the plurality of heating elements based on the corresponding print data row while the print medium is moved, thereby forming a line of dots on the print medium; and
repeating the sequential moving and the selective activating for each of the plurality of print data rows to form one or more complete letters on the print medium.

