A system for efficient hardware implementation of a perfect precision blending function, comprising:
an input interface configured to receive a plurality of input data operands, each having a defined input precision, and at least one blending factor having a defined blending factor precision;
a blending processing unit coupled to said input interface, said blending processing unit comprising dedicated hardware logic circuitry configured to:
    generate a first intermediate product by multiplying a first input data operand from said plurality of input data operands by said at least one blending factor;
    generate a second intermediate product by multiplying a second input data operand from said plurality of input data operands by a complement of said at least one blending factor;
    generate a preliminary blended result by adding said first intermediate product and said second intermediate product; and
    scale said preliminary blended result to a target output precision;
    wherein said dedicated hardware logic circuitry is configured to maintain an intermediate precision for said first intermediate product, said second intermediate product, and said preliminary blended result that is sufficient to prevent loss of significant bits from said input data operands and said blending factor during said multiplying and adding operations, thereby ensuring perfect precision blending; and
an output interface coupled to said blending processing unit, said output interface configured to provide a blended output data operand having said target output precision.

A semiconductor switching circuit comprising:
an input terminal configured to receive a control signal;
a drive circuit coupled to the input terminal and configured to generate an electrical signal based on the control signal;
an optical emitter coupled to the drive circuit and configured to emit light in response to the electrical signal;
an optical detector spatially separated from the optical emitter and configured to receive the emitted light and generate a detected electrical signal;
a semiconductor switching element coupled to the optical detector and configured to control current flow through an output path in response to the detected electrical signal; and
an output terminal coupled to the semiconductor switching element, wherein the optical emitter and the optical detector are galvanically isolated from each other.

A self-adjusting bit rate transducer for an optical transmission system, the transducer comprising:
    an optical input configured to receive an incoming optical signal;
    a bit rate detection unit coupled to the optical input, the bit rate detection unit configured to determine a current bit rate of the incoming optical signal;
    a processing unit coupled to the bit rate detection unit, the processing unit configured to determine a target bit rate for an outgoing optical signal based on the current bit rate of the incoming optical signal and at least one operating parameter of the optical transmission system;
    a bit rate conversion unit coupled to the processing unit, the bit rate conversion unit configured to convert the incoming optical signal to an outgoing optical signal having the determined target bit rate; and
    an optical output coupled to the bit rate conversion unit, the optical output configured to transmit the outgoing optical signal.

A system for detecting child presence, comprising:
