wherein the dimensions and arrangement of said metallic elements and apertures are configured to render the window substantially optically transparent to visible light and substantially transparent to millimeter-wave radiation in a millimeter-wave frequency range.

A method for compressing motion vectors of an unsynchronized picture, the method comprising:
    receiving motion vectors corresponding to blocks of an unsynchronized picture, wherein the unsynchronized picture is characterized by a lack of a standard temporal reference frame for motion vector prediction;
    determining, for a current block within the unsynchronized picture, a predicted motion vector for a current motion vector of said current block, said predicted motion vector being based on at least one of spatially neighboring motion vectors within the unsynchronized picture or motion vectors from a non-temporally aligned reference source;
    generating a motion vector difference by subtracting the predicted motion vector from the current motion vector; and
    encoding the motion vector difference to produce compressed motion vector data associated with the unsynchronized picture.

An automatic control circuit for enabling and disabling a supply voltage to a short-range wireless device, the circuit comprising:
a detection module configured to detect a predetermined short-range wireless communication trigger condition;
a controller operably coupled to the detection module, the controller configured to receive an input from the detection module and to determine, based on said input, whether to enable or disable the supply voltage; and
a power switching module operably coupled to the controller and configured to selectively provide the supply voltage to the short-range wireless device;
wherein the controller is further configured to activate the power switching module to enable the supply voltage to the short-range wireless device upon determining the presence of the predetermined short-range wireless communication trigger condition; and
wherein the controller is further configured to deactivate the power switching module to disable the supply voltage to the short-range wireless device upon determining the absence of the predetermined short-range wireless communication trigger condition for a predefined period.

A FinFET structure, comprising:
