a data storage configured to store the digitally signed data object and the digital credential in an associated manner; and
an object verification module configured to verify the authenticity and integrity of the digitally signed data object by utilizing the public key obtained from the associated digital credential to validate the digital signature.

What is claimed is:

A portable, collapsible workstation tray table apparatus, comprising:
a generally planar main support surface defining a working area for receiving items thereon;
a support frame pivotally coupled to the main support surface;
wherein the support frame is configured to selectively transition between an extended, operative configuration, in which the main support surface is supported at a working height above a ground surface, and a collapsed, stowed configuration, in which the apparatus occupies a reduced volume compared to the extended configuration;
wherein the main support surface is selectively adjustable in angular orientation relative to a horizontal plane when in the extended, operative configuration;
and wherein said collapsed, stowed configuration facilitates portable transport and compact storage of the apparatus.

A method of manufacturing a nano-template for a high-density patterned medium, comprising:
providing a substrate;
forming a template layer on the substrate;
patterning said template layer with a plurality of nanometer-scale features, wherein said features are arranged at a density suitable for fabricating a high-density patterned magnetic storage medium;
and processing the patterned template layer to form a durable nano-template configured for replicating said plurality of nanometer-scale features for a high-density patterned magnetic storage medium.

A cemented carbide cutting insert, comprising:
an insert body formed of a cemented carbide material, said insert body having at least one cutting edge;
an integral securing structure formed monolithically with said insert body and extending from a mounting surface thereof;
said integral securing structure configured to directly engage a complementary recess within a tool holder;
whereby said cutting insert is mechanically retained within the tool holder solely by the engagement of said integral securing structure with said complementary recess, without the requirement for a separate clamping element.

1. A turbidity sensor, comprising:
a housing configured to define a sample region for a fluid;
a light source positioned relative to the housing and configured to emit light into the sample region;
a light detector positioned relative to the housing and configured to receive light from the sample region after interaction with the fluid;
wherein the light detector is configured to generate an electrical signal indicative of a characteristic of the received light; and
a processor communicatively coupled to the light detector, the processor configured to determine a turbidity value of the fluid based on the electrical signal generated by the light detector.

An apparatus for fluid handling, comprising:
a main body defining an internal chamber configured for containing a fluid;
at least one inlet port in fluid communication with the internal chamber for introducing fluid therein;
at least one outlet port in fluid communication with the internal chamber for dispensing fluid therefrom;
a closure mechanism configured to seal an opening of the main body, thereby preventing leakage of the contained fluid;
wherein the main body is constructed from a chemically resistant material;
wherein the main body further comprises external indicia for volumetric measurement of the contained fluid; and
wherein the main body is dimensioned to be modularly compatible with laboratory fluidic systems, and further configured to be scaled to various capacities while maintaining functional integrity.;

A pressure balanced bearing comprising:
a first bearing member configured for rotation about an axis;
a second bearing member concentrically disposed relative to the first bearing member, defining an annular bearing interface therebetween;
a high-pressure fluid region disposed axially adjacent to a first end of the bearing interface, wherein fluid pressure within the high-pressure fluid region exerts an axial thrust force on the first bearing member in a first axial direction;
a balancing chamber defined between a portion of the first bearing member and a portion of the second bearing member, said balancing chamber being axially opposite the high-pressure fluid region relative to the bearing interface;
a pressure balancing surface formed on the first bearing member and exposed to fluid pressure within the balancing chamber, said balancing surface having an effective area such that fluid pressure within the balancing chamber exerts a counter-thrust force on the first bearing member in a second axial direction, opposite to the first axial direction; and
a fluid communication passage connecting the high-pressure fluid region to the balancing chamber, thereby introducing fluid from the high-pressure fluid region into the balancing chamber;
wherein the counter-thrust force substantially offsets the axial thrust force to achieve pressure balancing across the bearing.

1.  A method for maximizing efficiency of a multi-user communications network, the method comprising:
    acquiring a plurality of operational parameters indicative of network performance and user demand across a plurality of user devices within the multi-user communications network;
    determining, based on said plurality of operational parameters, a set of optimization objectives for improving network efficiency, wherein said set of optimization objectives comprises at least two conflicting objectives selected from a group consisting of: network throughput, latency, energy consumption, and user fairness;
    generating, by a network controller, a dynamic resource allocation strategy configured to concurrently optimize said at least two conflicting objectives, wherein said dynamic resource allocation strategy comprises an assignment of communication resources including at least one of bandwidth, transmit power, and time slots to said plurality of user devices;
    transmitting, from the network controller, instructions to a plurality of network nodes to implement said dynamic resource allocation strategy; and
    continuously adapting said dynamic resource allocation strategy based on subsequent acquisitions of said plurality of operational parameters to maintain optimized network efficiency.

1. An illumination structure comprising:
a housing defining an enclosure;
at least one light-emitting element disposed within the housing;
an electrical power interface electrically coupled to the at least one light-emitting element, the electrical power interface configured to receive electrical power to energize the at least one light-emitting element; and
at least one optical element coupled to the housing and positioned to modify light emitted from the at least one light-emitting element.

CLAIM 1.
A fuel supply device for a motorcycle, the device comprising:
a fuel tank configured to store fuel;
a filler opening fluidly coupled to the fuel tank, the filler opening configured to receive fuel into the fuel tank;
a fuel pump configured to draw fuel from the fuel tank;
a fuel filter fluidly coupled downstream of the fuel pump;
a fuel delivery line fluidly connecting the fuel filter to a fuel supply interface of a motorcycle engine; and
wherein the fuel pump is configured to supply pressurized fuel from the fuel tank, through the fuel filter and the fuel delivery line, to the fuel supply interface of the motorcycle engine.

A gas particle partitioner, comprising:
a housing defining an internal chamber;
an inlet port configured to receive a gas stream comprising gas and entrained particles into the internal chamber;
a separation element positioned within the internal chamber and configured to partition the gas stream into a substantially particle-free gas stream and a particle-enriched stream;
a first outlet port configured to discharge the substantially particle-free gas stream from the internal chamber; and
a second outlet port configured to discharge the particle-enriched stream from the internal chamber.

An adjustable scribe block, comprising:
a base having a reference surface adapted to engage a workpiece;
a vertically oriented column slidably engaged with the base;
the column comprising a distal end configured to receive a scribing element;
a scribing element detachably coupled to the distal end of the column; and
a locking mechanism configured to selectively secure the column at a desired vertical position relative to the base, whereby a distance between a tip of the scribing element and the reference surface of the base is adjustable.

A method for site-selective electrochemical deposition of copper, comprising:
providing a substrate;
selectively defining at least one deposition site on the substrate surface;
immersing the substrate in an electrolyte solution comprising copper ions; and
applying an electrochemical potential between the substrate and a counter electrode to cause selective deposition of copper onto the at least one defined deposition site.

1. An apparatus comprising:
    a line definition mechanism configured to establish a linear path having an ascertainable direction and a measurable length;
    a bearing determination module operatively associated with the line definition mechanism, said bearing determination module configured to ascertain an angular orientation of said linear path relative to a reference;
    a range determination module operatively associated with the line definition mechanism, said range determination module configured to measure a distance along said linear path;
    and an output interface configured to communicate said angular orientation and said distance.

An oil pressure warning system for an outboard motor, comprising:
an oil pressure sensor configured to detect oil pressure within an oil lubrication system of the outboard motor;
a controller coupled to the oil pressure sensor, said controller configured to receive a signal from the oil pressure sensor and to compare the detected oil pressure to a predetermined threshold;
a warning indicator coupled to the controller and positioned to be visible or audible to an operator of the outboard motor; and
wherein the controller is further configured to activate the warning indicator when the detected oil pressure falls below the predetermined threshold.

A system to construct an improved view of a process, the system comprising:
