A system for unified web hosting and content distribution, comprising:
at least one origin server configured to host web content and application logic;
a content distribution network communicatively coupled to the at least one origin server, the content distribution network comprising a plurality of edge nodes geographically distributed and configured to cache and serve web content to end-users;
a performance level data store configured to store a plurality of predetermined performance levels, each predetermined performance level defining a target performance characteristic for at least a portion of the web content or application logic;
a performance monitoring engine configured to monitor actual performance metrics of the unified web hosting and content distribution system, the actual performance metrics including, without limitation, network latency, data throughput, and content availability, from a plurality of geographic monitoring points; and
a performance assurance controller communicatively coupled to the performance level data store, the performance monitoring engine, the at least one origin server, and the content distribution network, the performance assurance controller configured to compare the monitored actual performance metrics with the stored predetermined performance levels and, in response to determining that an actual performance metric does not meet a corresponding predetermined performance level, dynamically initiate an adjustment to at least one operational parameter of the unified web hosting and content distribution system, wherein the adjustment is selected from a group comprising: modification of content caching policies, reallocation of computing resources, modification of data routing paths, and activation of additional network capacity, thereby assuring that the actual performance metrics meet or exceed the predetermined performance levels.

A method for intelligent congestion feedback, comprising:
monitoring a plurality of operational metrics indicative of potential congestion within a system;
intelligently analyzing said plurality of operational metrics to detect a congestion event and determine at least one characteristic of said congestion event;
generating a feedback message based on said detected congestion event and said at least one characteristic, said feedback message comprising specific guidance for mitigating said congestion event; and
transmitting said feedback message to at least one recipient for implementing said specific guidance.

A method for seeking images based on content, the method comprising:
for each of a plurality of images in a database, determining overall image content features and identifying at least one region of interest within the respective image;
for each identified region of interest, extracting a set of region-specific content features from the respective region of interest;
receiving an image search query;
generating query content features from the received image search query, the generated query content features comprising at least one of overall query content features and query region-specific content features;
comparing the generated query content features with the determined overall image content features of the plurality of images and with the extracted region-specific content features of the at least one region of interest from each respective image;
identifying at least one image from the plurality of images that satisfies the image search query based on said comparison; and
presenting the at least one identified image as a search result.

A method for streamlining execution of emulated code, the method comprising:
    receiving, by an emulation system, emulated code configured to run on a target processor architecture;
    identifying a basic block within the emulated code, wherein the basic block comprises a sequence of emulated instructions without any control flow transfers except at an end of the sequence;
    translating the identified basic block from the target processor architecture into a corresponding native code block for a host processor architecture;
    storing the native code block in a translation cache associated with the emulation system;
    executing the native code block on the host processor architecture; and
    subsequently, upon detecting that the basic block is to be executed again, retrieving the stored native code block from the translation cache for execution without re-translating the basic block.

A method for digital content spatial replacement, comprising:
