a fluid pressure source fluidly coupled to the internal cavity of the reinforcement member;
a sealing mechanism configured to seal the internal cavity of the reinforcement member;
wherein, upon introduction of fluid under pressure from the fluid pressure source into the sealed internal cavity, the reinforcement member is configured to expand radially outwardly, thereby exerting a reinforcing force against the structural component and conforming the outer surface of the reinforcement member to the surface of the structural component.

A control circuit for an LED driver, the control circuit comprising:
a power input configured to receive an input power signal;
a sensing module configured to detect an operating parameter of an LED string coupled to the LED driver, the operating parameter including at least one of an LED current and an LED voltage;
a control unit coupled to the sensing module, the control unit configured to generate a control signal based on a comparison between the detected operating parameter and a predetermined reference parameter; and
an output driver coupled to the control unit, the output driver configured to generate an output drive signal for controlling the LED driver circuit, wherein the output drive signal regulates the operating parameter of the LED string to maintain it substantially at the predetermined reference parameter.

A packet-based integrated circuit dynamic random access memory (DRAM) device, comprising:
a DRAM array structured into rows and columns for storing data;
an on-chip row register cache integrated with the DRAM array; and
packet processing circuitry coupled to the DRAM array and the on-chip row register cache;
wherein the packet processing circuitry is configured to receive memory access requests as packets; to retrieve data from a selected row of the DRAM array into the on-chip row register cache upon an initial access to the selected row; and to provide data from the on-chip row register cache in response to subsequent memory access requests for data within the selected row, thereby reducing data access latencies.

A semiconductor interconnect comprising:
