a compound spinal rod having a longitudinal axis and a first portion and a second portion;
the first portion and the second portion comprising different materials or having different mechanical properties along the longitudinal axis;
the compound spinal rod configured to be received and secured by the deflectable post of the bone anchor;
the compound spinal rod further configured to distribute biomechanical loads across multiple vertebral segments, thereby providing a low profile spinal prosthesis for stabilization of a spinal segment.

A DC to DC converter assembly, comprising:
