A method for low bias estimation of a signal-to-noise ratio (SNR) under small SNR conditions, the method comprising:
receiving a composite signal comprising a signal component and a noise component;
obtaining a first statistical measure representing a total power of the composite signal;
obtaining a second statistical measure representing a noise power of the noise component;
employing an estimation function that combines the first statistical measure and the second statistical measure to produce an estimated signal-to-noise ratio, wherein the estimation function is specifically configured to mitigate estimation bias that arises when the signal-to-noise ratio is small; and
outputting the estimated signal-to-noise ratio as a low-bias estimate.

A marine propulsion system with efficient engine speed control, comprising:
at least one marine engine configured to generate rotational power;
at least one propeller operatively coupled to the at least one marine engine;
a shaft system connecting the at least one marine engine to the at least one propeller;
at least one engine speed sensor configured to detect an actual engine speed of the at least one marine engine;
at least one operational parameter sensor configured to detect at least one operational parameter indicative of a vessel operating condition; and
a propulsion control unit (PCU) in operative communication with the at least one marine engine, the PCU configured to;
    receive the actual engine speed from the at least one engine speed sensor;
    receive the at least one operational parameter from the at least one operational parameter sensor;
    determine a target engine speed based on the actual engine speed, the at least one operational parameter, and a pre-defined efficiency criterion;
    calculate a target engine speed delta, representing a difference between the actual engine speed and the determined target engine speed, such that adjusting the actual engine speed by the target engine speed delta moves the engine towards an optimal operating point according to the efficiency criterion; and
    generate an engine control signal to adjust the actual engine speed of the at least one marine engine in accordance with the calculated target engine speed delta, thereby efficiently optimizing at least one of fuel consumption, power delivery, or emissions.

A method for reducing communication errors in a wireless communication system, comprising:
