establishing one or more bandwidth allocation policies, said policies defining criteria for assigning bandwidth among the plurality of entities for the plurality of shared resources;
assigning a portion of the total available bandwidth from each requested shared resource to each requesting entity based on the one or more bandwidth allocation policies;
monitoring actual bandwidth usage by each of the plurality of entities for each of the plurality of shared resources; and
dynamically modifying the allocated bandwidth for at least one of the plurality of entities for at least one of the plurality of shared resources based on the monitored actual bandwidth usage and the one or more bandwidth allocation policies;
thereby reducing bandwidth contention and optimizing resource performance.

A method for side impact testing of motor vehicles at a sub-system level, comprising:
