correlating, by the computing system, the raw vulnerability scan results with the obtained contextual information for identifying superfluous findings or false positives from the raw vulnerability scan results, wherein a superfluous finding or false positive is identified when a reported potential vulnerability fails to align with an actual configuration or operational state of a corresponding target asset;
generating, by the computing system, refined vulnerability scan results through filtering out said identified superfluous findings or false positives from the raw vulnerability scan results; and
providing, by the computing system, the refined vulnerability scan results for presentation, storage, or subsequent automated remediation actions.

