A system for the dispensing of medical products, comprising:
a product storage unit adapted to hold multiple medical products;
a product identification module arranged to identify a selected medical product from said stored medical products;
a dispensing mechanism functionally connected to the product storage unit, which retrieves and dispenses the selected medical product;
a dosage control unit adapted to govern the quantity of the selected medical product dispensed;
a user interface to receive input pertinent to a desired dispensing action; and
a control unit communicatively linked to the product identification module, the dispensing mechanism, the dosage control unit, and the user interface, and configured to manage the dispensing operation responsive to said received input.

A method for mitigating group delay effects in transmit beamforming radio communication, comprising:
producing a plurality of beamforming signals for transmission through a plurality of transmit paths;
determining group delay characteristics for each of the plurality of transmit paths;
computing a compensation to address group delay disparities among the plurality of transmit paths, based on said determined group delay characteristics; and
implementing said compensation to at least one of the plurality of beamforming signals to thereby equalize the group delays across the plurality of transmit paths.

1. An apparatus for separating water from a fluid stream derived from an oil and gas well, the apparatus comprising:
    an inlet adapted to receive the fluid stream, which includes oil, gas, and water;
    a separation chamber in fluid communication with the inlet;
    a filtering element positioned within the separation chamber, the filtering element operative to separate an aqueous phase from a hydrocarbon phase of said fluid stream;
    a first outlet arranged to discharge the separated aqueous phase; and
    a second outlet arranged to discharge the filtered hydrocarbon phase.

A polymer fiber exhibiting enhanced ballistic performance;
the polymer fiber comprising a polymeric material whose molecular structure is characterized by a high degree of orientation and crystallinity;
wherein such high degree of orientation and crystallinity confers upon the polymer fiber a tensile strength of at least 2.0 GPa and a tensile modulus of at least 50 GPa;
thereby enabling the polymer fiber to dissipate kinetic energy from ballistic impact with greater efficacy than a conventional polymer fiber.

A video recording apparatus having embedded program guide capabilities, comprising:
a tuner configured to acquire broadcast video signals;
a recording module coupled to the tuner, configured to capture designated segments of the broadcast video signals;
a data storage medium coupled to the recording module, configured to archive the recorded video signals;
a reproduction module coupled to the data storage medium, configured to play back the archived video signals;
a video output interface configured to render video signals for display on an external viewing device;
an EPG data receiver configured to obtain electronic program guide (EPG) data;
an EPG data repository coupled to the EPG data receiver, configured to store the EPG data;
a program guide display generator coupled to the EPG data repository and the video output interface, configured to produce a graphical representation of the EPG data for presentation on the external viewing device; and
a control unit coupled to the tuner, the recording module, the reproduction module, the EPG data receiver, the EPG data repository, and the program guide display generator, wherein the control unit is configured to facilitate user selection of a program from the graphical representation of the EPG data, and to autonomously schedule and commence recording of the selected program through the recording module and the tuner, based on said user selection and the EPG data.

A vinyl siding panel comprising:
an elongated panel body formed from a polymeric material;
said panel body having a visible face surface, a top edge, and a bottom edge;
wherein the visible face surface is substantially planar vertically, presenting a generally flat aesthetic upon installation, and substantially lacking a downwardly angled lap profile or a rounded dutch lap profile typical of conventional siding designs;
the top edge forming a nailing hem extending upwardly and rearwardly from the visible face surface, said nailing hem with a plurality of apertures adapted for receiving fasteners to attach the panel to a substrate;
the bottom edge featuring an upwardly extending locking butt configured to interlock with a complementary locking feature of an adjacent, lower siding panel;
whereby engagement of the locking butt with the complementary locking feature places the visible face surface of the panel in substantially the same plane as the visible face surface of the adjacent lower siding panel, such that an overall flat appearance is maintained over multiple installed panels; and
wherein the nailing hem and the locking butt are configured to accommodate thermal expansion and contraction of the polymeric material while preserving the substantially planar aesthetic of the visible face surface.

A system for altering a functionality of an image processing device responsive to a file associated with a network application, comprising:
an image processing device configured to perform at least one image processing function;
a network interface operatively coupled to the image processing device, the network interface configured to receive a file associated with a network application;
a processor operatively coupled to the network interface and the image processing device, the processor configured to receive the file from the network interface, examine the file to determine a functional modification for the image processing device, and modify a functionality of the image processing device based on the determined functional modification; and
a memory operatively coupled to the processor, the memory storing instructions executable by the processor to perform the analysis and modification.

1. A guide wire comprising:
   an elongate shaft with a proximal and a distal end;
   said elongate shaft being flexible to allow for navigation through a tortuous pathway;
   said elongate shaft comprising a core element extending along at least a portion of its length for providing pushability and torque transmission;
   a distal tip situated at the distal end of said elongate shaft, said distal tip configured for atraumatic advancement within a body lumen;
   wherein the guide wire is adapted to facilitate insertion and guidance of a medical device through a body lumen.

A method for steering incoming packets in virtual networks, comprising:
receiving, by a host computing device having a plurality of virtual machines and a hypervisor, a network packet from a physical network interface;
identifying, from header information of the network packet, a virtual destination within a virtual network linked to at least one of the plurality of virtual machines;
determining a receive steering path for the network packet to the identified virtual destination, wherein the receive steering path provides a direct data route that bypasses at least one software-based packet processing component of the hypervisor; and
guiding the network packet according to the determined receive steering path to the identified virtual destination.

A device for producing and directing a cold air atmospheric pressure micro plasma jet, comprising:
a cold air supply arranged to supply cold air;
a plasma generation chamber fluidically coupled to the cold air supply, wherein the chamber is adapted to sustain an atmospheric pressure environment;
at least one electrode disposed within or adjacent to the plasma generation chamber, said at least one electrode electrically connected to a power supply;
wherein the power supply is operative to energize the at least one electrode to produce plasma from the cold air within the atmospheric pressure environment of the plasma generation chamber; and
a nozzle adapted to channel the generated plasma as a micro plasma jet for application.

1. An apparatus for organic vapor jet deposition, comprising:
   an organic material source adapted to generate an organic vapor;
   a jet nozzle fluidically coupled to the organic vapor source, the jet nozzle adapted to form a directed jet of the organic vapor;
   a deposition chamber including a substrate holder arranged to position a substrate for receipt of the organic vapor jet thereon; and
   a vacuum system coupled to the deposition chamber, adapted to maintain a reduced pressure within the deposition chamber.

A method for identifying distinct alternative paths between two object sets within heterogeneous data, the method comprising:
accessing heterogeneous data comprising a plurality of objects and relationships therebetween, said heterogeneous data existing in at least one of a 2D or a 3D form;
identifying a first object set and a second object set within said accessed heterogeneous data;
generating a plurality of candidate paths, each candidate path linking an object from the first object set to an object from the second object set via one or more intermediate objects and their respective relationships within the heterogeneous data;
filtering the plurality of candidate paths to identify distinct alternative paths based on predefined criteria of distinctness and alternativeness;
and outputting the identified distinct alternative paths.

1. A system for streaming media, including:
    a media content repository configured to store various media files;
    a media processing unit operatively connected to the media content repository, said media processing unit adapted to encode or transcode one or more of said media files into multiple streamable data segments, wherein each streamable data segment is linked to a particular media quality level;
    a streaming delivery module operatively connected to the media processing unit, said streaming delivery module configured to receive a media request from a client device, select one or more of said streamable data segments corresponding to the requested media, and transmit said one or more streamable data segments to the client device over a communication network based on prevailing network conditions; and
    a client device in communication with the streaming delivery module via the communication network, said client device comprising:
        a network interface adapted to receive the transmitted streamable data segments;
        a buffer arranged to temporarily hold the received streamable data segments; and
        a media playback engine configured to decode and render the buffered streamable data segments for user presentation.

A satellite communication system, comprising:
a ground segment including a first communication unit;
a space segment including a second communication unit housed within a satellite;
wherein the first communication unit transmits data to the second communication unit via an uplink, and the second communication unit transmits data to the first communication unit or another ground segment via a downlink;
at least one Low Density Parity Check (LDPC) encoder within the system, adapted to encode data utilizing an LDPC coding scheme to generate LDPC encoded data;
at least one LDPC decoder within the system, adapted to decode the LDPC encoded data utilizing the LDPC coding scheme to restore original data; and
wherein the LDPC encoded data is conveyed across at least one of the uplink or the downlink.

A method for managing handoff in a wireless communication system, the method comprising:
    observing, by a user equipment or a network entity, a signal characteristic pertaining to a wireless connection between the user equipment and a serving base station;
    selecting, based on the observed signal characteristic, one or more candidate target base stations for a prospective handoff of the user equipment;
    assessing, by a network entity or the user equipment, a necessity for a handoff of the user equipment from the serving base station to a chosen one of the one or more candidate target base stations;
    commencing a handoff procedure to transition the wireless connection of the user equipment from the serving base station to the chosen target base station; and
    finalizing the handoff procedure, thus establishing the wireless connection of the user equipment with the chosen target base station.

1. A method of mass spectrometry, comprising:
    introducing a sample into an ionization zone;
    ionizing at least a segment of the sample to produce a plurality of ions;
    directing the plurality of ions to a mass analyzer;
    resolving the plurality of ions in the mass analyzer based on their mass-to-charge ratio; and
    detecting the resolved ions to acquire mass spectral data.

An insulating glass (IG) window assembly comprising:
a first glass pane;
a second glass pane;
a spacer situated between said first glass pane and said second glass pane, thereby defining a sealed insulating cavity between said spacer and said panes;
a heat treatable coating applied to a surface of at least one of said first glass pane and said second glass pane;
wherein said heat treatable coating is adapted to endure a heat treatment process without substantial degradation of its optical or thermal characteristics;
and wherein said heat treatable coating includes at least one layer of silicon-rich silicon nitride.

A data communication equipment, comprising:
a communication interface configured for transmitting data to and receiving data from an external communication medium;
a processor coupled to the communication interface;
and a memory coupled to the processor, the memory storing instructions executable by the processor to manage operation of the communication interface, to handle data received through the communication interface, and to format data for transmission via the communication interface.

A speech recognition system, comprising:
an audio input module configured to acquire speech audio signals;
a feature extraction module coupled to the audio input module, configured to transform said speech audio signals into a sequence of acoustic features;
an acoustic model coupled to the feature extraction module, configured to produce acoustic likelihoods for sub-word units based on said sequence of acoustic features;
a vocabulary database containing a multitude of words surpassing a threshold size typical of conventional speech recognition systems, wherein said vocabulary database is structured for efficient access and retrieval of its individual words and their corresponding sub-word units;
a language model, coupled to said vocabulary database, configured to forecast sequences of words from said vocabulary database, wherein said language model employs a hierarchical or statistical compression scheme to efficiently manage said multitude of words;
a decoder, coupled to said acoustic model, said language model, and said vocabulary database, configured to derive a sequence of recognized words using said acoustic likelihoods and said language model, wherein said decoder employs a multi-pass search strategy with dynamic pruning to efficiently traverse a search space defined by said expansive vocabulary database; and
an output module coupled to said decoder, configured to furnish said sequence of recognized words.

A method of continuously casting thin strip, comprising:
supplying a source of molten metal;
introducing said molten metal into a casting mold, wherein said casting mold comprises a pair of opposing surfaces spaced apart, thereby defining a casting gap corresponding to a predetermined thickness of said thin strip;
solidifying at least a portion of said molten metal within said casting mold to form said thin strip;
continuously withdrawing said thin strip from said casting mold;
and further cooling said thin strip subsequent to its withdrawal from said casting mold.

Claim 1. A system comprising:
A light control module for aviation obstruction marking, the module comprising:
a control circuit arranged to execute light operation logic;
an ambient light sensor coupled to said control circuit and configured to generate a light intensity signal indicative of ambient light conditions;
an output interface coupled to said control circuit and arranged to deliver power and control signals to at least one aviation obstruction light fixture;
a power supply arranged to furnish operating power to said control circuit and said output interface; and
an enclosure enclosing said control circuit, said ambient light sensor, said output interface, and said power supply;
wherein said control circuit is further configured to receive said light intensity signal and, responsive to said light intensity signal, generate said control signals for operating said at least one aviation obstruction light fixture in accordance with a predetermined aviation marking standard.

A gear wheel, comprising:
a central hub portion adapted for securing the gear wheel to a rotating shaft;
an outer rim portion featuring a plurality of external gear teeth suited for meshing engagement with a complementary gear;
a plurality of spokes spanning radially between the central hub portion and the outer rim portion, said spokes establishing an internal structural geometry within the gear wheel;
wherein at least one of said central hub portion, outer rim portion, or spokes comprises a composite material construction, said composite material construction comprising a load-bearing fiber matrix embedded within a polymer or metal alloy body, engineered to provide a high strength-to-weight ratio;
consequently allowing for reduced mass and enhanced durability of the gear wheel during operation within a gear system.

A method for fabricating a semiconductor device, comprising:
furnishing a semiconductor substrate;
forming a first active region having a first semiconductor material upon the semiconductor substrate;
forming a second active region having a second semiconductor material upon the first active region;
wherein at least one of said forming steps employs a controlled deposition process configured to achieve a desired material property or a particular interface characteristic between the first active region and the second active region;
structuring at least one of the first active region or the second active region to define a functional component of the semiconductor device; and
forming electrical contacts electrically coupled to the functional component, thus fabricating the semiconductor device.

A cord severing mechanism for a tire cord applicator head, comprising:
a severing element adapted to cut a tire cord;
an actuator coupled to the severing element for moving the severing element along a cutting path;
a support structure configured to mount the severing element and the actuator to the tire cord applicator head;
a cord support surface positioned to receive the tire cord and cooperate with the severing element to facilitate tire cord severance; and
a control unit configured to selectively actuate the actuator to effect severing of the tire cord.

A gear transmission, comprising:
multiple gears;
at least one input shaft, wherein said input shaft is operatively connected to at least one of the multiple gears to impart rotational power thereto;
at least one output shaft, wherein said output shaft is operatively connected to at least one of the multiple gears to obtain rotational power therefrom; and
wherein the multiple gears are operatively engaged with one another to convey rotational power from the at least one input shaft to the at least one output shaft.

A method for fabricating a metal-insulator-metal (MIM) capacitor, said method comprising:
providing a substrate;
forming a first metal layer on the substrate, the first metal layer serving as a bottom electrode of the MIM capacitor;
depositing an insulating dielectric layer over the first metal layer;
forming a second metal layer on the insulating dielectric layer, said second metal layer comprising a top electrode of the MIM capacitor;
depositing a covering dielectric layer over the second metal layer and any exposed portions of the insulating dielectric layer;
forming a passivation layer atop the covering dielectric layer.

A liquid crystal display comprising:
a first substrate;
a second substrate arranged opposite the first substrate;
a liquid crystal layer situated between the first substrate and the second substrate;
a first electrode provided on an inner surface of the first substrate;
a second electrode provided on an inner surface of the second substrate;
said first and second electrodes configured to generate an electric field across the liquid crystal layer, thereby selectively modulating light transmitted through or reflected by the liquid crystal layer;
a first polarizer located on an outer surface of the first substrate;
a second polarizer located on an outer surface of the second substrate;
a first alignment layer situated between the first substrate and the liquid crystal layer, said first alignment layer adapted to align liquid crystal molecules within the liquid crystal layer; and
a second alignment layer situated between the second substrate and the liquid crystal layer, said second alignment layer adapted to align liquid crystal molecules within the liquid crystal layer;
wherein said selective modulation of light forms a display image.

A method for fabricating a high current capable bipolar transistor comprising:
furnishing a semiconductor substrate comprising a buried collector layer;
depositing an epitaxial layer atop the buried collector layer;
selectively etching at least one deep trench through the epitaxial layer to the buried collector layer, where the deep trench delineates a deep collector region within the epitaxial layer and establishes a low-resistance current path to the buried collector layer;
creating a base region within the epitaxial layer, situated laterally adjacent to the deep collector region delineated by the deep trench;
establishing an emitter region within the base region;
and subsequently creating electrical contacts to the emitter region, the base region, and the deep collector region.

An apparatus for controlling braking force of a motor vehicle, comprising:
a brake pedal sensor arranged to produce a brake demand signal responsive to driver input;
a plurality of wheel speed sensors arranged to provide wheel speed signals indicative of rotational speeds of individual wheels of the motor vehicle;
a brake actuator system arranged to apply a braking force to at least one wheel of the motor vehicle; and
a controller operably coupled to the brake pedal sensor, the plurality of wheel speed sensors, and the brake actuator system, the controller operative to receive the brake demand signal from the brake pedal sensor and the wheel speed signals from the plurality of wheel speed sensors, to ascertain a target braking force based at least in part on the brake demand signal, to compute an actual braking force applied to the at least one wheel based at least in part on the wheel speed signals, to compare the target braking force with the actual braking force, and to produce a control signal for the brake actuator system for adjusting, based on the comparison, the braking force applied to the at least one wheel, thereby controlling the braking force of the motor vehicle.

A system for dynamically delivering information to a user, comprising:
a user device adapted to receive and display information;
a global positioning system (GPS) receiver coupled to the user device, adapted to generate real-time geographical location data indicative of the user device's position;
a remote server configured to maintain a collection of information items;
a communication network configured to enable data exchange between the user device and the remote server;
wherein the remote server is further adapted to obtain the real-time geographical location data from the user device;
wherein the remote server is further adapted to dynamically select at least one information item from the collection of information items based on the obtained real-time geographical location data; and
wherein the remote server is further adapted to transmit the selected at least one information item to the user device via the communication network without an express request for the information item from the user device.

An apparatus for in-situ fuel injector calibration in an internal combustion engine, comprising:
an internal combustion engine;
at least one fuel injector configured to inject fuel into the internal combustion engine;
a plurality of sensors configured to generate signals indicative of engine operating parameters during operation of the engine; and
an engine control unit (ECU) communicatively coupled to the at least one fuel injector and the plurality of sensors, the ECU comprising processing circuitry configured to:
receive the sensor signals;
determine, based on the received sensor signals, at least one actual fuel delivery characteristic of the at least one fuel injector during engine operation;
calculate at least one calibration parameter for the at least one fuel injector based on the at least one determined actual fuel delivery characteristic and a desired fuel delivery characteristic; and
adjust a control signal provided to the at least one fuel injector based on the at least one calculated calibration parameter to modify fuel delivery from the at least one fuel injector during subsequent engine operation.

An optical detection system for liquid samples, comprising:
a light source configured to emit light;
a sample holder adapted to contain a liquid sample, the sample holder being positioned so that the emitted light interacts with the liquid sample;
a detector configured to receive light having interacted with the liquid sample; and
a processing unit coupled to the detector, said processing unit arranged to analyze a signal from the detector to ascertain at least one characteristic of the liquid sample.

A construction machine, comprising:
a frame;
a propulsion system connected to the frame, adapted to move the construction machine over a surface;
a power source attached to the frame, arranged to supply operational energy;
a working implement affixed to the frame, adapted for performing a construction task;
an actuation system linked to the working implement, arranged to manipulate the working implement; and
a control system adapted to control the propulsion system and the actuation system.

1. A closing unit for an injection moulding machine, the closing unit comprising:
   a fixed platen adapted to receive a first mould half;
   a movable platen adapted to receive a second mould half;
   at least two tie bars interconnecting the fixed platen and the movable platen, the tie bars guiding the movement of the movable platen;
   and a clamping mechanism mechanically coupled to at least one of the fixed platen and the movable platen, the clamping mechanism adapted to displace the movable platen between an open position and a closed position and to exert a clamping force on the first and second mould halves when in the closed position.

A loudspeaker comprising:
a frame;
a magnet assembly affixed to the frame, the magnet assembly forming an annular magnetic gap;
a diaphragm possessing a central portion and an outer perimeter;
a suspension system positioned between the outer perimeter of the diaphragm and the frame; and
a voice coil assembly coupled to the central portion of the diaphragm, the voice coil assembly including a coil former having an electrically conductive winding wound thereon, wherein the voice coil assembly is situated within the annular magnetic gap.

A method for presenting map locations within a user application, the method comprising:
obtaining, by a computing device executing said user application, a Uniform Resource Locator (URL) string;
identifying, by the computing device, geographic map location data corresponding to the obtained URL string;
creating, by the computing device, a map view derived from the identified geographic map location data, configured for presentation within the user application;
and presenting, by the computing device, the created map view within a graphical user interface of said user application, wherein the presented map view illustrates the geographic map location.

A fuel blend for a diesel engine, comprising:
a base diesel fuel;
a cetane improver, in an amount sufficient to elevate the cetane number of the base diesel fuel;
a cold flow improver, at a level effective to enhance the low-temperature operability of the base diesel fuel; and
a detergent additive, in an amount effective to mitigate or prevent deposit formation within the diesel engine.

An electro-optical device comprising:
an electrical interface arranged to transmit or receive an electrical signal;
an optical interface arranged to transmit or receive an optical signal;
an electro-optical conversion element coupled between the electrical interface and the optical interface, said element operable to convert an electrical signal into an optical signal, convert an optical signal into an electrical signal, or modulate an optical signal based on an electrical signal;
a power unit electrically connected to the electro-optical conversion element; and
an enclosure containing the electrical interface, the optical interface, and the electro-optical conversion element.

1. A method for assessing the status of or diagnosing a pancreatic B-cell associated autoimmune disease in a subject, comprising:
    providing a biological sample from the subject;
    measuring in the biological sample the presence or level of at least one biomarker suggestive of pancreatic B-cell autoimmunity;
    comparing the measured presence or level of the at least one biomarker to an established reference value; and
    ascertaining, from the comparison, the status of a pancreatic B-cell associated autoimmune disease in the subject.

A memory array, comprising:
    a semiconductor substrate;
    multiple memory cells disposed over the semiconductor substrate;
    an isolation region located within the semiconductor substrate; and
    a digit line electrically connected to at least one of the multiple memory cells, said digit line being embedded within the isolation region;

A flow measuring apparatus, comprising:
a conduit defining a fluid passage;
a constriction element positioned within the fluid passage, said constriction element creating a restricted cross-sectional area through which fluid moves;
a deflectable membrane operatively connected to the constriction element such that the deflectable membrane is subjected to a pressure differential generated across the constriction element by fluid movement;
and a sensing element arranged to detect deflection of the deflectable membrane and to produce a signal representative of a flow rate through the fluid passage based on the detected deflection.

A standard interface rack, comprising:
a frame structure providing a plurality of standardized mounting bays;
a power distribution system integrated into the frame structure, said power distribution system comprising a plurality of standardized power connectors positioned within each of said plurality of standardized mounting bays, said standardized power connectors configured to provide electrical power to electronic modules adapted for insertion into the mounting bays;
a data communication system integrated into the frame structure, said data communication system comprising a plurality of standardized data connectors positioned within each of said plurality of standardized mounting bays, said standardized data connectors configured to facilitate data communication among electronic modules adapted for insertion into the mounting bays and with external systems; and
each of said plurality of standardized mounting bays configured to mechanically and electrically accommodate distinct electronic modules compliant with a predefined interoperability standard, thereby facilitating interchangeability and interoperability among the distinct electronic modules.

A method for determining the relative likelihood of failures, comprising:
determining a plurality of potential failure events pertaining to a system or process;
acquiring data reflecting failure conditions or characteristics for each of the plurality of potential failure events;
calculating, for each determined potential failure event, a distinct likelihood score based on said acquired data;
evaluating the distinct likelihood scores among the plurality of potential failure events to ascertain a relative likelihood for each determined potential failure event; and
producing an output representative of the ascertained relative likelihoods.

1. A system for haptic confirmation of commands, the system comprising:
    an input interface adapted to obtain a user command;
    a processor communicatively coupled to the input interface, said processor operative to:
        process the received user command; and
        identify a haptic feedback profile associated with the user command;
    a haptic feedback generator communicatively coupled to the processor, the haptic feedback generator operative to produce a haptic sensation based on the identified haptic feedback profile;
    wherein the generated haptic sensation conveys a haptic confirmation of the user command to the user.

A high-voltage NMOS transistor, comprising:
a semiconductor substrate having a first conductivity type;
a gate electrode disposed over the semiconductor substrate;
a gate dielectric layer situated between the gate electrode and the semiconductor substrate, said gate dielectric layer possessing a thickness configured to withstand breakdown voltages exceeding a predetermined low-voltage threshold;
a source region of a second conductivity type established within the semiconductor substrate, laterally adjacent to a first side of the gate electrode;
a drain region of the second conductivity type established within the semiconductor substrate, laterally separated from a second side of the gate electrode; and
an extended drain drift region of the second conductivity type, less heavily doped than the drain region, situated within the semiconductor substrate between a channel region beneath the gate electrode and the drain region, said extended drain drift region adapted to sustain high drain-to-source voltages.

A method for depositing a metal oxide film, comprising:
  providing a substrate within a reaction chamber;
  introducing a metal-containing precursor into the reaction chamber;
  introducing an oxygen-containing precursor into the reaction chamber;
  maintaining the substrate at a temperature suitable for film formation; and
  reacting the metal-containing precursor with the oxygen-containing precursor on a surface of the substrate to deposit the metal oxide film.

A method for localizing a sound source to enable online calibration of auditory cue to location transformations, comprising:
obtaining a plurality of sound signals emanating from a sound source, where each signal is received by a distinct sensor at a separate location;
deriving at least one auditory cue from the received sound signals, the at least one auditory cue indicative of a spatial property of the sound source;
determining an initial position of the sound source utilizing the at least one auditory cue and a current set of auditory cue to location transformations;
calculating a difference between the determined initial position and a reference position of the sound source, where the reference position is independently established or known; and
modifying the current set of auditory cue to location transformations in response to the calculated difference, thereby achieving online calibration of the auditory cue to location transformations.

A programmable controller, including:
a processor adapted to execute program instructions and process data;
a memory coupled to the processor, said memory storing the program instructions and data;
an input interface coupled to the processor, said input interface configured to receive input signals from one or more external devices;
an output interface coupled to the processor, said output interface configured to generate output control signals for one or more external devices; and
wherein the processor is configured to execute said stored program instructions based on the received input signals and the stored data, to generate output control signals for controlling the operation of the one or more external devices.

An information recovery method, comprising:
receiving a data stream that includes encoded data;
evaluating the received data stream to ascertain one or more encoding attributes of the encoded data;
choosing a decoding scheme from a set of available decoding schemes according to the ascertained encoding attribute;
decoding the encoded data via the chosen decoding scheme to produce decoded information; and
presenting the decoded information in a perceptible form.

A computing system comprising:
a volatile memory configured to store dynamic data;
a non-volatile flash memory configured to store persistent data;
a control unit communicatively coupled to the volatile memory and the non-volatile flash memory;
wherein the control unit is configured to:
detect a trigger event signaling a forthcoming alteration in power state or an operating condition impacting data retention within the volatile memory;
in response to detecting the trigger event, initiate a back-up operation to autonomously transfer the dynamic data from the volatile memory to the non-volatile flash memory for enduring preservation;
subsequently detect a recovery event signaling a resumption of an operational state; and
in response to detecting the recovery event, initiate a restoration operation to autonomously transfer the persistent data from the non-volatile flash memory back to the volatile memory;
thereby enabling uninterrupted safeguarding and retrieval of the dynamic data during the power state alteration or operating condition.

A method for producing and processing a material slab, including the steps of:
forming a raw material into an elongated slab;
continuously conveying the elongated slab from a forming station to a processing station;
performing at least one processing operation on the elongated slab at the processing station, wherein said at least one processing operation comprises at least one of cutting, shaping, or surface treating the elongated slab; and
collecting discrete slab portions subsequent to said performing at least one processing operation;

A method of charging a battery, the method comprising:
providing a charging current and/or voltage to the battery;
monitoring one or more operating parameters of the battery, said one or more operating parameters comprising at least one of battery voltage, battery current, battery temperature, or battery state of charge;
adaptively modifying one or more charging parameters of the provided charging current and/or voltage in response to the monitored operating parameter;
wherein said adaptive modification is performed to optimize one or more of charging speed, battery longevity, or battery safety.

1. An organic light emitting device, comprising:
   a substrate;
   an anode positioned above the substrate;
   a cathode disposed over the anode; and
   an organic layer stack interposed between the anode and the cathode, said organic layer stack comprising at least one hole transport layer, an organic light emitting layer, and at least one electron transport layer;
   wherein the organic light emitting device is adapted to emit light responsive to an electrical current between the anode and the cathode.

1. A method for fabricating chip-scale semiconductor packages, the method comprising:
    providing a plurality of semiconductor dice;
    providing a substrate panel comprising a plurality of package sites;
    securing each of the plurality of semiconductor dice to a corresponding package site on the substrate panel in a flip-chip configuration;
    dispensing an underfill material between each of the plurality of semiconductor dice and the substrate panel;
    curing the underfill material;
    forming an encapsulant over the plurality of semiconductor dice and portions of the substrate panel, wherein the encapsulant is configured to extend only minimally beyond lateral edges of the corresponding semiconductor dice;
    forming a plurality of external electrical contacts on a bottom surface of the substrate panel, each plurality of external electrical contacts being electrically coupled to a respective semiconductor die, and being configured to be substantially co-extensive with a footprint of that respective semiconductor die; and
    singulating the substrate panel into a plurality of individual chip-scale semiconductor packages.

An immersion lithographic apparatus, comprising:
a projection system arranged to cast a patterned radiation beam onto a substrate;
a substrate stage adapted to retain the substrate;
an immersion liquid supply system arranged to furnish an immersion fluid to a region between the projection system and the substrate;
and a pressure sensor adapted to sense the pressure of the immersion fluid within the region between the projection system and the substrate.

A radiofrequency amplifier, comprising:
a radiofrequency input port configured to accept an incoming radiofrequency signal;
a radiofrequency output port configured to deliver an amplified radiofrequency output signal;
an active amplifying component operatively connected between the radiofrequency input port and the radiofrequency output port, wherein the active amplifying component amplifies the input radiofrequency signal;
a biasing circuit configured to supply operating power to the active amplifying component;
an input impedance matching network interposed between the radiofrequency input port and an input of the active amplifying component, the input impedance matching network structured to align the impedance of the radiofrequency input port with an input impedance of the active amplifying component; and
an output impedance matching network connected between an output of the active amplifying component and the radiofrequency output port, the output impedance matching network arranged to align an output impedance of the active amplifying component with the impedance of the radiofrequency output port.

An apparatus, comprising:
a voltage generator;
wherein said voltage generator is configured to provide a variable voltage drop;
said variable voltage drop representing the voltage drop of at least one of a memory cell, a current mirror circuit, and a replica circuit.

1. An apparatus for delivering cooling and heating employing waste heat, comprising:
    a waste heat source;
    a thermal energy extraction unit arranged to transfer thermal energy from said waste heat source to a working fluid;
    a cooling subsystem operatively coupled to said thermal energy extraction unit and adapted to provide a cooling effect;
    a heating subsystem operatively coupled to said thermal energy extraction unit and adapted to provide a heating effect; and
    a control system arranged to control the functioning of said thermal energy extraction unit, said cooling subsystem, and said heating subsystem for selectively furnishing said cooling effect, said heating effect, or both, in response to sensed operational parameters and a defined demand.

An electronic device comprising:
a processing unit arranged to perform instructions;
a memory unit communicatively coupled to the processing unit and arranged to store instructions and data;
multiple sensors arranged to sense environmental conditions and/or user interaction pertaining to the electronic device;
a power management unit communicatively coupled to the processing unit and arranged to manage power supply to diverse components of the electronic device;
wherein the processing unit is additionally arranged to:
obtain historical usage data of the electronic device and sensor data from said multiple sensors;
process the obtained historical usage data and sensor data to formulate a forecast for future usage profiles or power requirements of the electronic device;
create a power management command in view of the forecast; and
send the power management command to the power management unit, wherein said power management unit is additionally arranged to modify one or more operational parameters of the electronic device upon receipt of said power management command to enhance power efficiency.

A system for magnetically securing optical components upon a bench for solder attachment, the system comprising:
a bench platform;
a reconfigurable optical component fixture arranged on the bench platform;
at least one magnetic element integrated within or coupled to the reconfigurable optical component fixture; and
at least one optical component having a magnetically responsive feature adapted to interact with the at least one magnetic element;
wherein the at least one magnetic element is configured to steadfastly retain the at least one optical component in a defined orientation and position relative to the bench platform for a solder attachment process; and
further wherein the reconfigurable optical component fixture is arranged to permit unobstructed access to a solderable interface of the at least one optical component during the solder attachment process.

A method for enhanced fabrication of a semiconductor device, the method comprising:
providing a semiconductor substrate comprising a region intended for device formation;
creating at least one stress-inducing structure adjacent to the region of the semiconductor substrate;
producing a localized stress field within the region of the semiconductor substrate by means of the at least one stress-inducing structure; and
altering at least one material property, electrical property, or structural characteristic of the semiconductor substrate within said region by said localized stress field to enhance device performance or reliability.

A memory circuit comprising:
a field effect transistor (FET) serving as a memory cell, said FET comprising a gate, a source, and a drain;
wherein said FET is adapted to store a data state through a threshold voltage shift determined by a stored charge;
a word line electrically connected to the gate of said FET;
a bit line electrically connected to either the source or the drain of said FET; and
control circuitry adapted to apply voltages to the word line and the bit line for programming, reading, or erasing the data state held within said FET.

An apparatus for timing recovery in a wireless transceiver, comprising:
a receiver adapted to acquire an incident wireless signal;
a sampler arranged to sample the incident wireless signal, thereby generating sampled data at a sampling rate governed by a sampling clock;
a timing error detector coupled to said sampler, said timing error detector operative to generate a timing error signal derived from the sampled data, said timing error signal reflecting a timing disparity between the sampling clock and a symbol timing of the incident wireless signal;
a loop filter coupled to said timing error detector, said loop filter adapted to filter the timing error signal, thereby producing a filtered timing error signal; and
a clock recovery unit coupled to said loop filter, said clock recovery unit arranged to modify the sampling clock in response to the filtered timing error signal, thereby aligning the sampling clock with the symbol timing of the incident wireless signal.

A pluggable drive carrier assembly comprising:
a carrier housing adapted to house and secure a data storage drive therein;
an electrical connector situated on a rear section of the carrier housing, the electrical connector arranged to electrically connect with a complementary connector on a backplane upon insertion of the carrier housing into a drive bay;
a retention mechanism attached to the carrier housing, the retention mechanism adapted to selectively retain the carrier housing within the drive bay and enable tool-free extraction of the carrier housing therefrom; and
at least one guide feature located on an external surface of the carrier housing, the at least one guide feature arranged to interface with a complementary guide feature within the drive bay to aid alignment during insertion and withdrawal of the carrier housing.

An apparatus for creating an ultra-small spot, comprising:
a source adapted to produce an energy beam;
a focusing assembly functionally connected to said source and adapted to receive said energy beam, said focusing assembly incorporating at least one high numerical aperture element and structured to converge said energy beam onto a target plane;
wherein said focusing assembly is additionally arranged to create a spot at said target plane possessing a characteristic dimension significantly less than a diffraction limit of said energy beam; and
a control system functionally connected to at least one of said source and said focusing assembly, configured to manage the emission and focusing of said energy beam.

A method for producing a storage tank for gas and liquid, comprising:
shaping a main body portion of the tank from a sheet material;
shaping at least one end closure for the tank from a sheet material;
connecting the at least one end closure to the main body portion along a seam to form a closed vessel;
sealing the seam to ensure a leak-tight state of the closed vessel; and
pressurizing the closed vessel to a designated test pressure to confirm its structural integrity and leak-tightness.

1. A method of manufacturing a semiconductor device, comprising:
obtaining a substrate;
forming over the substrate at least one semiconductor layer;
forming at least one device structure within or upon the at least one semiconductor layer; and
subsequently forming at least one interconnect structure electrically coupled to the at least one device structure.

A method for detecting chronic stress or a related disorder in an individual, comprising:
acquiring a biological sample from the individual;
measuring a level of at least one biomarker associated with chronic stress or a related disorder in the biological sample;
comparing said measured level of the at least one biomarker to a predetermined reference level; and
identifying the individual as having chronic stress or a related disorder based on a deviation of said measured level from said reference level.

1. A method for fabricating semiconductor structures having contact holes, comprising:
    providing a semiconductor substrate;
    depositing a dielectric layer over the semiconductor substrate;
    creating a patterned mask layer over the dielectric layer, wherein the patterned mask layer delineates at least one opening at a desired contact hole location;
    etching through the dielectric layer via the at least one opening in the patterned mask layer, thereby forming at least one contact hole, the at least one contact hole extending through the dielectric layer to expose an underlying portion of the semiconductor substrate or an underlying conductive film;
    populating the at least one contact hole with a conductive material.

A Schottky diode comprising:
a semiconductor substrate of a first conductivity type having a first surface and an opposing second surface;
an ohmic contact situated on the first surface of the semiconductor substrate;
a Schottky metal layer situated on the second surface of the semiconductor substrate, which forms a rectifying contact with the semiconductor substrate;
a localized high-doping region of the first conductivity type integrated into the semiconductor substrate directly beneath and contacting a central portion of the Schottky metal layer, this localized high-doping region being configured to diminish an effective Schottky barrier height, thereby enhancing forward current of the Schottky diode;
and a field termination structure integrated into the semiconductor substrate positioned peripheral to the localized high-doping region and encircling the rectifying contact, this field termination structure being configured to alleviate electric field crowding at an edge of the rectifying contact, thereby enhancing reverse bias characteristics of the Schottky diode.

A method for producing a power semiconductor device, comprising:
providing a semiconductor substrate;
forming a voltage sustaining layer on the semiconductor substrate;
creating a terraced trench within the voltage sustaining layer, the terraced trench exhibiting a plurality of laterally offset steps along at least one sidewall thereof, said steps delineating a varying depth profile into the voltage sustaining layer;
introducing a dielectric material into the terraced trench to form a trench isolation region; and
forming a plurality of floating islands in the voltage sustaining layer, wherein the plurality of floating islands are physically isolated from each other by the trench isolation region.

A display control device comprising:
a display unit configured to present a graphical user interface (GUI);
an input unit configured to receive user input data;
a processor coupled to the display unit and the input unit;
a memory coupled to the processor and storing program instructions;
wherein the processor, in response to executing the program instructions, is configured to:
generate graphical elements comprising the GUI for display on the display unit;
determine a device state or an environmental parameter; and
dynamically modify at least one visual attribute or interactive functionality of one or more of the graphical elements based on the determined device state or the environmental parameter.

A method for treating a substrate, comprising:
obtaining a substrate designated for treatment;
ascertaining one or more treatment parameters for the obtained substrate;
producing a set of machine-executable control instructions utilizing the one or more ascertained treatment parameters; and
actuating a substrate treatment apparatus to effect a treatment upon the substrate in accordance with the produced set of machine-executable control instructions.

A rotation-angle-detecting apparatus, comprising:
    a rotatable member adapted to rotate about an axis;
    a stationary member disposed relative to the rotatable member;
    a sensing arrangement operative to generate a signal reflecting a relative angular position between the rotatable member and the stationary member;
    a processing unit electronically coupled with the sensing arrangement, the processing unit adapted to ascertain the rotational angle of the rotatable member from the generated signal; and
    an output interface adapted to furnish said determined rotation angle.

1. An imaging apparatus, comprising:
a light source configured to project light towards a subject;
an optical system configured to receive light reflected or transmitted from the subject and subsequently form an image;
an image sensor configured to capture the image formed by the optical system and generate corresponding image data; and
a processor configured to receive the image data from the image sensor and produce an output image.

A coupling comprising:
a first coupling member having a recessed receiving portion with an internal engagement surface;
a second coupling member having an insertable male portion with an external engagement surface, said male portion being structured to cooperatively engage said recessed receiving portion;
a plurality of radially translatable locking elements arranged circumferentially within said first coupling member, each of said locking elements resiliently urged by a spring mechanism towards an extended position;
an annular groove formed on said external engagement surface of said male portion, dimensioned to receive said extended locking elements, thereby securing said first coupling member to said second coupling member; and
an actuation collar slidably mounted on said first coupling member, said actuation collar adapted to selectively retract said locking elements from said annular groove, allowing disengagement of said male portion from said recessed receiving portion.

A method for cutting food products, including:
    delivering a food product to a cutting station;
    orienting the food product relative to at least one cutting element;
    activating said at least one cutting element to engage and sever the food product along a predefined cutting path;
    isolating the severed portions of the food product from any remaining unsevered parts; and
    removing the severed portions from the cutting station.

A jig for positioning a door hinge for mounting to a vehicle via an automated mounting system, said jig comprising:
a main body;
a hinge reception portion formed with the main body, said hinge reception portion configured to securely receive and hold the door hinge in a specific orientation;
at least one vehicle interface element projecting from the main body, said at least one vehicle interface element configured to accurately engage a datum surface of the vehicle body to achieve a fixed alignment of the jig relative to the vehicle; and
an automated system interface portion formed with the main body, said automated system interface portion configured to mechanically connect with an end effector of the automated system for manipulating and controlling the jig;
wherein, when the door hinge is received in the hinge reception portion and the at least one vehicle interface element engages the datum surface of the vehicle body, the door hinge is maintained in a precise mounting position relative to the vehicle for subsequent attachment by the automated system.

An apparatus for controlling a sliding and hinged sun roof, comprising:
a user input device configured to receive a user command for a sun roof panel, said user command specifying a desired movement chosen from a sliding action and a hinging action;
a control unit electronically coupled to the user input device, said control unit configured to interpret the received user command;
a sun roof assembly comprising a sun roof panel, a sliding rail system for facilitating the sliding movement of the sun roof panel relative to a roof opening, and a hinge mechanism for facilitating the hinging movement of the sun roof panel relative to said roof opening;
at least one actuator mechanically connected to the sun roof assembly and electrically coupled to the control unit;
wherein the control unit is further configured to actuate the at least one actuator to effectuate the desired movement of the sun roof panel, such that the sun roof panel either executes the sliding movement along the sliding rail system or engages in the hinging movement through the hinge mechanism, in accordance with the interpreted user command.

A firearm trigger mechanism, comprising:
a housing adapted for mounting within a firearm frame;
a trigger pivotally disposed within the housing, said trigger comprising an engagement surface;
a sear pivotally disposed within the housing, said sear arranged to engage a hammer or striker of the firearm, the sear being mechanically linked to the engagement surface of the trigger;
a trigger pull weight adjustment mechanism, comprising an adjustment screw threadably engaged with the housing and arranged to apply adjustable pressure on a spring biasing at least one of the trigger and the sear;
a trigger travel adjustment mechanism, comprising at least one adjustment screw threadably engaged with the housing and adapted to restrict a range of pivotal motion of the trigger;
wherein rotation of the adjustment screw of the trigger pull weight adjustment mechanism alters the force needed to disengage the sear from the hammer or striker; and
wherein rotation of the at least one adjustment screw of the trigger travel adjustment mechanism modifies the travel distance of the trigger.

A method for extruding a tire rubber compound, comprising:
supplying a pre-mixed, unvulcanized tire rubber compound at a predetermined temperature;
feeding the pre-mixed, unvulcanized tire rubber compound into an extruder equipped with at least one screw for plasticizing and pressurizing the compound;
expelling the plasticized and pressurized tire rubber compound through a shaping die to form an extruded profile having a predefined cross-sectional shape suitable for a tire component;
cooling the extruded profile while retaining its predefined cross-sectional shape; and
retrieving the cooled extruded profile.

A method for dynamic flow-based multi-path load balancing with quality of service guarantees, comprising:
  receiving network traffic including a plurality of data flows;
  determining a plurality of available network paths for transmitting the network traffic;
  assigning a quality of service (QoS) requirement to each of the plurality of data flows;
  dynamically observing performance characteristics for each of the plurality of available network paths, wherein said performance characteristics comprise at least current load and available bandwidth;
  dynamically selecting a target network path for each data flow from the plurality of available network paths by assessing the associated QoS requirement of the respective data flow against the dynamically observed performance characteristics of the plurality of available network paths, whereby the selection provides the associated QoS guarantee for the respective data flow while balancing network traffic load across the plurality of available network paths;
  forwarding each data flow along its respective target network path.

A system for determining location using a machine-to-machine (M2M) ecosystem, comprising:
a target M2M device coupled to an asset whose geographical position is to be ascertained;
a plurality of anchor M2M devices deployed within a defined area, each such anchor M2M device having a known or determinable geographical position;
an M2M communication network communicatively linked to the target M2M device and the plurality of anchor M2M devices, said network enabling the exchange of location-related data between the target M2M device and the plurality of anchor M2M devices; and
a location determination unit communicatively coupled to the M2M communication network, said unit configured to acquire the location-related data from the target M2M device and the plurality of anchor M2M devices, and subsequently compute a current geographical location of the asset based on the acquired location-related data.

A semiconductor memory device, comprising:
a main memory array including multiple memory cells organized in rows and columns;
a redundant memory array including multiple redundant memory cells;
a defect address storage circuit adapted to store one or more addresses indicating a faulty memory location within the main memory array;
an address input circuit operative to receive an input address to access a memory location; and
an address control circuit interconnected with the address input circuit, the defect address storage circuit, the main memory array, and the redundant memory array, configured to compare the input address with the one or more stored defective addresses and, if a match occurs, select a memory location within the redundant memory array for access, bypassing the faulty memory location within the main memory array, and if no match occurs, select a memory location within the main memory array for access.

A method for evaluating electrical cables, comprising:
exposing an electrical cable to a penetrating energy beam;
obtaining projection data by detecting the penetrating energy beam subsequent to its passage through the electrical cable, said obtaining being conducted from multiple angular positions about a longitudinal axis of the electrical cable;
creating a tomographic reconstruction of a cross-sectional image of the electrical cable utilizing the obtained projection data;
examining the tomographic reconstruction to determine a structural characteristic, degradation, or imperfection within the electrical cable; and
producing a diagnostic assessment of the electrical cable utilizing the determined structural characteristic, degradation, or imperfection.

A system for ship propulsion, the system comprising:
an airborne rigid kite body configured to produce aerodynamic lift and drag forces upon exposure to an airflow;
an on-board power plant coupled to the rigid kite body, said power plant adapted to generate power for operating at least one component of the airborne rigid kite body;
at least one active thrust generating mechanism coupled to the rigid kite body and driven by the on-board power plant, said active thrust generating mechanism configured to augment propulsive forces generated by the rigid kite body;
a tether having a first end coupled to the rigid kite body and a second end adapted to be coupled to a ship, said tether configured to transmit propulsive forces from the rigid kite body to the ship; and
a control system configured to regulate flight parameters of the rigid kite body to optimize propulsive forces transmitted via the tether.

A computer-implemented method for an integrated system-of-systems modeling environment, the method comprising:
    providing a graphical user interface configured to enable user definition and configuration of a plurality of heterogeneous constituent systems, wherein each constituent system is independently operable and possesses distinct functionalities;
    receiving, via the graphical user interface, system definitions for each of the plurality of heterogeneous constituent systems;
    receiving, via the graphical user interface, interaction definitions detailing interdependencies, communication protocols, and interface specifications among the plurality of heterogeneous constituent systems;
    constructing a plurality of individual system models based on the received system definitions, wherein each individual system model represents the behavior of a respective constituent system;
    integrating the plurality of individual system models and the received interaction definitions into a unified system-of-systems (SoS) model, wherein the unified SoS model is configured to represent a combined operational behavior and emergent properties resulting from the interactions of the plurality of heterogeneous constituent systems;
    executing the unified SoS model to simulate a dynamic behavior of the SoS under at least one specified scenario;
    analyzing simulation outputs from the executed unified SoS model to identify performance characteristics or emergent properties of the SoS that are not readily apparent from individual constituent system models; and
    presenting, via the graphical user interface, simulation results and analysis outputs pertaining to the dynamic behavior, performance characteristics, or emergent properties of the SoS.

A system for a vehicle, comprising:
a display device located within the vehicle;
a plurality of input devices, each input device adapted to acquire user input from a distinct user within the vehicle;
a processor operatively coupled to the display device and the plurality of input devices; and
a memory operatively coupled to the processor and storing program instructions which, when executed by the processor, cause the processor to perform operations comprising:
render a graphical user interface on the display device;
present a plurality of cursors within the graphical user interface, wherein each cursor is associated with a corresponding one of the plurality of input devices;
obtain input from each of the plurality of input devices;
manage a position and/or state of each respective cursor on the display device based on the input received from its associated input device; and
enable interaction with at least one vehicle function or at least one graphical element of the graphical user interface via at least one of the plurality of cursors.

A method for client-side scaling of web server farms within a cloud data center, said method comprising:
acquiring, by a client device, server characteristic data from a plurality of web servers forming a web server farm operating within a cloud data center, wherein the server characteristic data reflects an operational status or resource capacity of each such web server;
the client device determining a request distribution strategy for the plurality of web servers utilizing the acquired server characteristic data;
the client device transmitting one or more web requests to at least one of the web servers in accordance with the determined request distribution strategy; and
periodically re-obtaining said server characteristic data and re-evaluating the request distribution strategy to dynamically adapt web request routing in response to changes in the operational status or resource capacity of the plurality of web servers.

A system for dynamically managing resource allocation within a data processing environment, said system comprising:
a resource monitoring module configured to collect real-time usage metrics for a plurality of computing resources within the data processing system and to gather demand data from a plurality of applications operating within the data processing system;
a resource analysis module operatively coupled to the resource monitoring module, said resource analysis module configured to process the collected usage metrics and demand data for identifying resource contention or underutilization, and, based on this analysis, to ascertain an adjusted allocation scheme for the plurality of computing resources; and
a resource allocation module interfaced with the resource analysis module, said resource allocation module configured to implement the adjusted allocation scheme to govern the distribution of the plurality of computing resources among the plurality of applications;
wherein the resource monitoring module, the resource analysis module, and the resource allocation module are arranged to function in a continuous feedback loop for adaptively modifying resource assignments based on evolving usage and demand conditions.

An electrically conductive article, comprising:
an electrically conductive thermoplastic elastomer composition;
wherein said composition comprises:
from about 50 wt% to about 99 wt% of at least one thermoplastic elastomer;
from about 1 wt% to about 50 wt% of at least one electrically conductive filler; and
optionally, one or more additional additives chosen from the group consisting of plasticizers, stabilizers, processing aids, flame retardants, colorants, or combinations thereof;
wherein said composition exhibits an electrical volume resistivity below about 10^9 ohm-cm; and
wherein said article is fabricated from said composition.

A pump system comprising:
a main pump having a suction inlet and a discharge outlet, adapted to transfer a liquid;
a priming circuit fluidly coupled to said main pump, said priming circuit comprising a priming pump and a priming valve, said priming pump arranged to extract air from at least one of said suction inlet and a housing of said main pump;
a sensor adapted to ascertain a priming status of said main pump, said priming status including at least one of fluid presence at said suction inlet and a vacuum magnitude within said main pump housing; and
a controller operatively linked to said sensor, said priming pump, and said priming valve, said controller arranged to automatically energize said priming pump and regulate said priming valve responsive to said detected priming status, wherein said regulation of said priming valve aids in evacuating air from said main pump to facilitate priming thereof.

A system comprising:
an elongate insertion tube with a distal end and a proximal end, the elongate insertion tube adapted for placement within a body lumen;
an illumination device situated at the distal end of the elongate insertion tube, the illumination device adapted to project light for illuminating an area outside the distal end;
an image acquisition device positioned at the distal end of the elongate insertion tube, the image acquisition device configured to acquire images of the illuminated area;
a processing unit electronically linked to the image acquisition device, the processing unit configured to obtain and process the acquired images; and
a display unit electronically connected to the processing unit, the display unit configured to display the processed images to a user.

An apparatus for managing congestive heart disease, comprising:
a physiological sensor adapted to sense one or more physiological parameters indicative of congestive heart disease in a patient;
a controller communicatively coupled to the physiological sensor, said controller operative to analyze the one or more physiological parameters and, based on such analysis, determine a therapeutic intervention;
a therapy delivery unit operationally linked to the controller, said therapy delivery unit adapted to provide the determined therapeutic intervention to the patient.

A method for delayed emergency location determination and transmission, the method comprising:
identifying an emergency condition;
ascertaining a geographic position linked to the emergency condition;
deferring transmission of the ascertained geographic position and any related emergency information for a specified duration or until a predefined criterion is satisfied;
reporting the ascertained geographic position and any related emergency information to a designated recipient upon expiration of the specified duration or fulfillment of the predefined criterion.

A camera comprising:
a camera housing;
an optical system affixed to the camera housing for focusing incident light to form an image;
a film receiving and transport mechanism situated within the camera housing for receiving silver-salt film and for selectively positioning said silver-salt film within an image plane of the optical system;
an electronic image sensor situated within the camera housing configured to convert incident light into electrical signals, wherein said electronic image sensor is selectively positionable within an image plane of the optical system;
a shutter mechanism to selectively regulate exposure of either said silver-salt film or said electronic image sensor to light transmitted through the optical system;
a control unit arranged to selectively actuate said film receiving and transport mechanism and said shutter mechanism for silver-salt image acquisition or to selectively actuate said electronic image sensor and said shutter mechanism for electronic image acquisition; and
an electronic memory operatively connected to said electronic image sensor for retaining image data produced by said electronic image sensor.

1. A shift register, comprising:
    a series of cascaded stages, each stage having an input terminal and an output terminal;
    a data input terminal adapted to receive a primary data signal;
    at least one clock input terminal for receiving at least one clock signal;
    wherein each stage is configured to acquire a data input signal from an output terminal of a prior stage or the data input terminal;
    wherein each stage further comprises:
        a data storage element for storing a data quantity;
        and a control logic circuit connected to the data storage element, its input terminal, and the at least one clock input terminal, the control logic circuit arranged to:
            ingest the data input signal into the data storage element upon detection of a first phase of the at least one clock signal; and
            relay the stored data quantity from the data storage element to the output terminal of the stage upon detection of a second phase of the at least one clock signal;
    thereby sequentially propagating data quantities from the data input terminal through the series of cascaded stages, to produce a sequence of synchronized output signals at the respective stage output terminals.

1. A computer mainframe housing for a computer system, comprising:
    an enclosure body establishing an internal volume;
    a plurality of internal mounting structures positioned within the internal volume, these mounting structures configured to secure diverse computer components;
    a power supply bay integrated within the enclosure body, said power supply bay configured to accept a power supply unit;
    at least one ventilation aperture formed by the enclosure body, said ventilation aperture configured to promote airflow for cooling computer components;
    a plurality of external port apertures formed by the enclosure body, said external port apertures arranged to grant access to input/output connectors of computer components; and
    at least one removable access panel coupled to the enclosure body, this removable access panel configured to permit user access to the internal volume.

A time acquisition apparatus, comprising:
a radio frequency receiver adapted to receive a radio time signal;
a time information extractor operatively coupled to the radio frequency receiver, adapted to extract time information from the incoming radio time signal;
a timekeeping unit operatively coupled to the time information extractor, adapted to synchronize its internal clock using the extracted time information; and
an output interface operatively coupled to the timekeeping unit, adapted to output said synchronized time.

A retrofit clip for securely joining a first structural member to a second structural member, configured to resist lateral and uplift forces, comprising:
    a unitary body comprising a high-strength material;
    a first attachment portion projecting from the unitary body, arranged for mechanical coupling to the first structural member;
    a second attachment portion projecting from the unitary body, arranged for mechanical coupling to the second structural member, wherein the first attachment portion and the second attachment portion are disposed at a predetermined angle relative to each other;
    a plurality of fastener apertures formed through at least the first attachment portion and the second attachment portion, the apertures adapted to receive fasteners for securing the clip to the first and second structural members; and
    wherein the unitary body is designed for external mounting onto an existing structural connection between the first and second structural members, without necessitating disassembly or significant modification of the existing structural members.

A system for analyzing network issues based on traffic path measurements, said system comprising:
one or more traffic measurement units configured to collect network traffic data from a network, said network traffic data including information identifying the path of said traffic through said network;
a data storage device coupled to said one or more traffic measurement units and configured to retain said collected network traffic data;
a processing unit coupled to said data storage device and configured to process said stored network traffic data to detect network problems, said network problems comprising deviations from expected network behavior, network performance degradation, or network failures;
and an output unit coupled to said processing unit and configured to output an indication of said detected network problems.

A self-contained payment system configured to enable transactions employing digital vouchers, the system comprising:
at least one processing unit;
at least one memory unit operatively connected to the at least one processing unit, the at least one memory unit storing computer-executable instructions which, when executed by the at least one processing unit, effectuate operations comprising:
  administering a plurality of digital vouchers, where each digital voucher is uniquely identifiable and embodies a unit of intrinsic value within the system;
  upholding a ledger of user accounts, where each user account is linked to a specific user and records a current balance of digital vouchers for that user;
  releasing a quantity of the digital vouchers into circulation by crediting a designated user account with said quantity of digital vouchers;
  enabling transfer of a specified quantity of digital vouchers from a sending user account to a receiving user account within the system in response to a payment transaction request, said enabling comprising debiting the specified quantity from the sending user account and crediting the specified quantity to the receiving user account, thus adjusting their respective balances; and
  handling a redemption request for a quantity of digital vouchers from a user account, said handling involving debiting the requested quantity from the user account and retiring the debited quantity of digital vouchers from circulation within the system.

1. An electronic device for presenting broadcast programs, the device comprising:
a tuner configured to acquire a broadcast signal;
a processor coupled to the tuner;
a memory coupled to the processor, for storing processor-executable instructions;
an input interface coupled to the processor, configured to acquire user input; and
an output interface coupled to the processor, configured to present program content;
wherein the processor is configured to extract program content and corresponding program guide information from the broadcast signal; generate an interactive program guide display utilizing the corresponding program guide information; cause the output interface to render the interactive program guide display for a user; receive, through the input interface, a user selection of a broadcast program from the interactive program guide display; in response to said user selection, direct the tuner to tune to a broadcast channel associated with the chosen broadcast program; and cause the output interface to render the program content of the chosen broadcast program to the user.

A method for providing trunk service utilizing Long Term Evolution (LTE) and a trunk user terminal (TUT), the method comprising:
establishing, by the TUT, connectivity with an LTE network;
transmitting, by the TUT, a request to join a trunk group to a trunk service platform via the LTE network;
receiving, at the TUT, an indication confirming successful joining of the trunk group;
initiating, by the TUT, a push-to-talk (PTT) communication session through transmission of a PTT request signal to the trunk service platform via the LTE network;
receiving, at the trunk service platform, the PTT request signal;
establishing, by the LTE network, a dedicated radio bearer for the PTT communication session between the TUT and the trunk service platform, the dedicated radio bearer configured with quality of service (QoS) parameters tailored for real-time voice communication;
transmitting voice data, by the TUT, over the established dedicated radio bearer to the trunk service platform; and
distributing, by the trunk service platform, the transmitted voice data to one or more other trunk user terminals within the trunk group via the LTE network.

A solar thermal power plant comprising:
a solar circuit adapted to warm a heat transfer fluid;
a steam generation circuit arranged to produce steam from a working fluid;
wherein the solar circuit is fluidly connected to the steam generation circuit through at least one heat exchanger for indirect evaporation of the working fluid by the heat transfer fluid;
the solar circuit also including a bypass conduction path;
said bypass conduction path arranged to selectively direct at least a portion of the heat transfer fluid around at least one of a superheating stage and a steam generation stage within the solar circuit;
and at least one valve structured to regulate fluid flow through said bypass conduction path.

An information processing device, comprising:
a processor configured to receive various input data related to an operating environment, determine a current contextual state of said operating environment based on the received input data, select a processing operation from a plurality of available processing operations based on the determined current contextual state, and execute the selected processing operation;
a memory coupled to the processor and configured to store instructions executable by the processor for performing said determination, selection, and execution, and further to store data utilized in said determination, selection, and execution;
an input interface coupled to the processor and configured to receive the various input data; and
an output interface coupled to the processor and configured to output a result from the executed processing operation or a control signal based thereon.

A system for gyroscopic stabilization of a two-wheeled vehicle, the system comprising:
a vehicle frame with a front portion and a rear portion;
a front wheel rotatably coupled to the front portion of the vehicle frame;
a rear wheel rotatably coupled to the rear portion of the vehicle frame;
at least one gyroscopic stabilization unit, comprising a spinning mass, said at least one gyroscopic stabilization unit mounted on the vehicle frame;
at least one sensor adapted to detect an orientation of the two-wheeled vehicle; and
a control unit communicatively coupled to the at least one sensor and to the at least one gyroscopic stabilization unit, the control unit configured to obtain data from the at least one sensor and, responsive to the received data, activate the spinning mass of the at least one gyroscopic stabilization unit to generate a gyroscopic torque, wherein said gyroscopic torque is applied to the vehicle frame to counteract a lean of the two-wheeled vehicle.

An automated system suitable for use with diverse fluid circuits, comprising:
    a controller configured to analyze operational parameters and issue control commands;
    a plurality of sensors adapted for connection to a fluid circuit, the sensors providing sensor data indicative of fluid circuit parameters;
    a plurality of actuators arranged for connection to the fluid circuit, the actuators responding to the control commands to alter fluid flow characteristics within the fluid circuit;
    a memory containing a plurality of fluid circuit profiles, each profile comprising a set of operational parameters and control logic specific to a distinct type of fluid circuit;
    wherein the controller is further configured to:
    obtain an identification of a fluid circuit coupled to the system;
    choose one of the plurality of fluid circuit profiles from the memory based on the obtained identification; and
    dynamically adapt its processing of the sensor data and its issuance of the control commands in accordance with the selected fluid circuit profile to manage the coupled fluid circuit.

A display device comprising:
a display panel configured to present visual content;
a processing unit coupled to the display panel, the processing unit configured to produce display signals for the display panel;
at least one environmental sensor coupled to the processing unit, the environmental sensor arranged to sense at least one ambient condition proximate to the display device;
at least one user interaction sensor coupled to the processing unit, the user interaction sensor arranged to sense at least one user interaction with the display device; and
a memory unit coupled to the processing unit, the memory unit storing executable instructions for the processing unit, wherein the processing unit, upon executing said instructions, is further configured to dynamically modify at least one display parameter of the display panel based on the sensed ambient condition and the sensed user interaction, thereby enhancing the presentation of visual content.

A method for policy-based routing in a multi-homed computer, comprising:
obtaining network packets at said multi-homed computer;
consulting a plurality of routing policies maintained on said multi-homed computer;
assessing each received network packet in accordance with said plurality of routing policies utilizing one or more packet characteristics;
ascertaining an outgoing network interface from a plurality of network interfaces of said multi-homed computer for each said network packet, said ascertainment based on said assessment; and
forwarding each said network packet through the ascertained outgoing network interface.

An apparatus for mitigating undue suction in a swimming pool skimmer, the apparatus comprising:
a skimmer body adapted to receive water from a swimming pool, said body defining an internal volume and comprising a primary water outlet connected to a pump suction line;
a suction relief port formed within the skimmer body, said port establishing fluid communication between the internal volume of the skimmer body and an external environment;
a valve mechanism functionally coupled to the suction relief port, said mechanism operable between a closed state, wherein the suction relief port is sealed, and an open state, allowing ingress of ambient air into the internal volume; and
a float mechanism situated within the internal volume of the skimmer body and functionally connected to the valve mechanism, said float mechanism arranged to actuate the valve mechanism to its open state when the water level within the internal volume drops below a preset threshold, thereby introducing ambient air into the internal volume to lessen undue suction at the primary water outlet.

A method for fabricating a memory device, the method comprising:
providing a substrate;
forming a plurality of first electrodes on the substrate, said first electrodes extending substantially parallel along a first direction;
forming a reversible variable-resistance memory layer over the first electrodes; and
forming a plurality of second electrodes over the reversible variable-resistance memory layer, said second electrodes extending substantially parallel along a second direction, wherein the second direction is substantially orthogonal to the first direction, and whereby portions of the reversible variable-resistance memory layer are interposed between intersections of the first and second electrodes to form memory cells.

A method for adaptive quality of service pre-authorization in a network environment, the method comprising:
at a network node, receiving a request for a communication service, the request comprising a desired quality of service (QoS) requirement;
evaluating, before complete establishment of the communication service, an authorization status for said desired QoS requirement based on at least one real-time network condition parameter and at least one communication policy;
selectively allocating network resources relevant to the desired QoS requirement based on the evaluated authorization status;
forwarding the authorization status to a requesting user equipment or an alternative network entity; and
permitting or preventing subsequent establishment of the communication service based on the forwarded authorization status.

An antenna structure, comprising:
a support structure;
multiple radiating elements mechanically affixed to the support structure, each configured to transmit and/or receive electromagnetic signals;
and a feed network electrically linked to the multiple radiating elements, wherein the multiple radiating elements are spatially arranged on the support structure, thereby defining a plurality of distinct radiation sectors for covering various angular regions, and further wherein the feed network is configured to individually or group-address the multiple radiating elements to enable independent or coordinated operation of said distinct radiation sectors.

A battery management system, comprising:
a controller configured to execute battery management functions;
multiple sensors configured to measure at least one of the voltage, current, and temperature of a battery pack;
a switching circuit electrically coupled to the battery pack and controllable by the controller; and
a communication interface configured to transmit battery operational data and receive control commands;
wherein the controller is further configured to:
obtain data from the multiple sensors;
analyze the collected data to ascertain a condition of the battery pack, including at least one of its state of charge and its state of health;
control the switching circuit based on the ascertained condition of the battery pack to manage charging and discharging operations and to provide protection against irregular operating conditions; and
relay the ascertained condition of the battery pack and any identified irregular operating conditions via the communication interface.

A batch billing system comprising:
a data storage unit arranged to retain billing data, the billing data including numerous billing items, each billing item linked to an account;
a batch processing unit arranged to process said numerous billing items in a collective operation to produce billing outputs;
an input module arranged to accept a user's choice for applying a persistent status indicator to one or more chosen billing items;
a control module adapted to inhibit automatic resetting of said persistent status indicator for said one or more chosen billing items over several successive batch operations; and
wherein, once applied, said persistent status indicator affects subsequent processing of said one or more chosen billing items in later batch operations without needing re-application of the indicator.

A system for distributing files, comprising:
at least one server;
wherein the at least one server comprises:
a processor;
a memory operatively coupled to the processor, the memory maintaining a collection of files and processor-executable instructions;
a network interface in communication with the processor, configured to facilitate data communication over a network;
the processor configured, upon execution of the processor-executable instructions, to execute operations including:
obtaining, via the network interface, a target file request from a client device;
locating the target file within the collection of files maintained in the memory;
creating a transmission package for the target file; and
dispatching the transmission package comprising the target file to the client device via the network interface and across the network; and
at least one client device;
wherein the at least one client device includes:
a client processor;
a client memory in communication with the client processor;
a client network interface operatively connected to the client processor, to facilitate data exchange over the network;
the client processor configured, upon execution of client processor-executable instructions, to carry out operations including:
transmitting, via the client network interface, the target file request to the at least one server;
obtaining, via the client network interface, the transmission package containing the target file from the at least one server; and
persisting the acquired target file in the client memory.

A capacitor section for a dynamic random-access memory, comprising:
a semiconductor substrate;
a first capacitor electrode disposed over or within said semiconductor substrate;
a dielectric layer conformally situated over at least a part of said first capacitor electrode;
a second capacitor electrode disposed over said dielectric layer, said second capacitor electrode serving as a common cell plate for multiple capacitor sections; and
wherein said first capacitor electrode is formed with a three-dimensional geometry, said three-dimensional geometry arranged to maximize an effective charge storage surface area within a projected area on said semiconductor substrate.

A system for managing access to system management information, comprising:
a system information acquisition module configured to collect system management information from a plurality of system resources, such information comprising at least one of performance data, configuration settings, and event logs;
a data storage repository coupled to the system information acquisition module, the data storage repository configured to persistently store the collected system management information;
an access request interface configured to receive a request for system management information from a requesting entity, wherein the request specifies one or more criteria for filtering and/or presenting the system management information;
an information processing engine coupled to the data storage repository and the access request interface, the information processing engine configured to:
    analyze the received request;
    obtain system management information from said data storage repository according to the specified criteria; and
    format the obtained system management information into a designated output structure;
a communication interface coupled to the information processing engine, the communication interface configured to transmit the formatted system management information to the requesting entity.

A solid electrolytic capacitor comprising:
an anode comprising a porous body fashioned from a valve metal;
a dielectric layer comprising an oxide of said valve metal, disposed on a surface of said porous body;
a solid electrolyte layer comprising a conductive polymer, provided on said dielectric layer;
a cathode collector layer comprising a conductive material, situated atop said solid electrolyte layer; and
an anode terminal electrically coupled to said anode, and a cathode terminal electrically coupled to said cathode collector layer.

An ink jet recording apparatus, comprising:
    a recording head for ejecting ink through multiple nozzles;
    a heater coupled to the recording head and configured to heat the recording head;
    a temperature sensor disposed with the recording head and arranged to detect the recording head's temperature; and
    a control unit electrically connected to the heater and the temperature sensor, the control unit configured to receive the detected temperature from the temperature sensor and control operation of the heater to maintain the recording head's temperature substantially at a target level.

An angle sensor, comprising:
