An engine control unit comprising:
multiple input interfaces configured to acquire various sensor signals reflecting operational conditions of an internal combustion engine;
a processor operatively linked to the multiple input interfaces;
a memory electronically coupled to the processor, said memory holding executable instructions and engine operational parameters;
multiple output interfaces operatively linked to the processor and configured to produce various control signals for a plurality of engine actuators;
wherein the processor is arranged to execute the executable instructions to:
ascertain an engine operating state utilizing the acquired sensor signals;
retrieve the engine operating parameters contained in the memory responsive to the ascertained engine operating state;
compute a set of engine control parameters based on the engine operating state and the retrieved engine operating parameters; and
produce the control signals for the plurality of engine actuators informed by the computed engine control parameters to regulate operation of the internal combustion engine.

An amplifying apparatus, comprising:
