identifying operational parameters for each of the multiple coexisting wireless communication technologies;
detecting an interference condition existing between at least two of the multiple coexisting wireless communication technologies within the shared wireless communication environment;
analyzing the detected interference condition together with the identified operational parameters to formulate a technology-specific interference mitigation strategy; and
implementing the formulated technology-specific interference mitigation strategy on at least one of the multiple coexisting wireless communication technologies to mitigate the interference.

A system configured to transparently furnish stateful execution for a stateless application, the system comprising:
a processor;
a memory coupled to the processor;
an interception component configured to intercept data operations initiated by the stateless application;
a state capture component coupled to the interception component and configured to extract and record application state data based on the intercepted data operations;
a state repository coupled to the state capture component and configured to persistently store the captured application state data; and
a state management component coupled to the state repository and configured to, upon an execution trigger of the stateless application, reconstruct an execution context for the stateless application leveraging the persistently stored application state data, wherein the reconstruction of the execution context furnishes stateful execution transparently to the stateless application.

1. An authentication system, comprising:
