    a memory arranged to retain reference authentication data;
    a processor operatively connected to the input interface and the memory, said processor configured to compare the incoming authentication data against the reference authentication data to ascertain an authentication outcome; and
    an output interface adapted to convey the authentication outcome.

A method for transitioning an embedded private branch exchange (PBX) system to a personal computer, the method comprising:
