a plurality of passive component connection pads electrically connected to the second mounting region; and
a plurality of external connection terminals situated on the bottom surface, electrically connected to at least one of the plurality of chip connection pads and the plurality of passive component connection pads;
wherein the second mounting region includes a cavity formed within the carrier substrate, said cavity designed to house the passive electronic component.

A work machine, comprising:
a main body;
a blade operatively coupled to the main body;
at least one sensor adapted to detect a parameter indicative of a position or orientation of the blade with respect to a designated reference;
at least one actuator coupled to the blade and arranged to effect movement of the blade; and
a controller communicatively coupled to the at least one sensor and the at least one actuator, the controller adapted to receive said parameter from the at least one sensor, to evaluate the detected parameter against a target position or orientation for the blade, and to automatically generate and transmit a control signal to the at least one actuator to move the blade to adjust the position or orientation thereof toward the target position or orientation.

A molded rubber composition for a golf ball;
