    an engine mounting bracket arranged to receive and securely hold an outboard engine;
    a pivot assembly mechanically connecting the transom mounting bracket to the engine mounting bracket, the pivot assembly establishing a pivot axis around which the engine mounting bracket and a secured outboard engine are pivotally movable relative to the transom mounting bracket between a deployed operating position and a tilted position; and
    a locking mechanism arranged to selectively retain the engine mounting bracket in at least one of the deployed operating position and the tilted position.

A printed circuit board comprising:
a dielectric substrate;
a plurality of conductive layers disposed on or embedded within said dielectric substrate;
a plurality of differential signal trace pairs defined in at least one of said plurality of conductive layers, wherein each differential signal trace pair includes a first signal trace and a second signal trace;
wherein said first and second signal traces of each differential signal trace pair are closely coupled to ensure a substantially uniform characteristic differential impedance along their length; and
wherein said plurality of differential signal trace pairs are configured in a high-density arrangement on at least one of said conductive layers, featuring an inter-pair spacing between adjacent pairs that is smaller than a pre-defined multiple of an intra-pair spacing between said first and second signal traces, thereby facilitating the routing of a greater number of differential signal trace pairs within a given area of the printed circuit board.

A reproduction speed conversion apparatus, comprising:
a signal input structured to receive an input reproduction signal with a first reproduction speed;
a speed conversion unit coupled to the signal input, said speed conversion unit processing the input reproduction signal to generate an output reproduction signal having a second reproduction speed, where the second reproduction speed is distinct from the first reproduction speed;
a control unit coupled to the speed conversion unit, said control unit providing a speed control parameter to the speed conversion unit, the speed control parameter defining a relationship between the first reproduction speed and the second reproduction speed; and
a signal output coupled to the speed conversion unit, the signal output outputting the output reproduction signal.

A filter structure for a vehicle air conditioner, comprising:
