a filter element situated within the interior channel, the filter element arranged to extract impurities from air passing through the interior channel;
and a sealing member positioned along an outer edge of the filter housing, the sealing member adapted to contact a complementary surface of the air conditioning system to preclude air bypass around the filter element.

1. A composition comprising:
ascorbic acid or a pharmaceutically acceptable salt or ester thereof;
at least one stabilizing agent for the ascorbic acid or a pharmaceutically acceptable salt or ester thereof, said agent being present in an amount effective to mitigate degradation of the ascorbic acid or a pharmaceutically acceptable salt or ester thereof;
and a cosmetically, pharmaceutically, or nutraceutically suitable carrier.

An identity broker system, comprising:
a processor configured to:
obtain an authentication request from a user desiring access to a host service;
redirect the user to an identity provider external to the identity broker system for authentication;
obtain an authentication assertion from the identity provider, said assertion confirming successful authentication of the user by the identity provider;
verify the obtained authentication assertion; and
send an authorization signal to the host service, responsive to the verified authentication assertion, to authorize the user's access to the host service.

1. A high-density MOSFET array, comprising:
    a semiconductor substrate;
    a plurality of MOSFETs situated on the semiconductor substrate, wherein each MOSFET includes a channel region, a gate dielectric overlying the channel region, a gate electrode overlying the gate dielectric, and source/drain regions disposed in the semiconductor substrate flanking the gate electrode;
    gate sidewall spacers positioned adjacent to lateral sides of the gate electrode;
    an interlevel dielectric layer disposed over the plurality of MOSFETs;
    a plurality of self-aligned contacts extending through the interlevel dielectric layer, each self-aligned contact is electrically coupled to at least one of the source regions or the drain regions of the plurality of MOSFETs, wherein each self-aligned contact is laterally defined by the gate sidewall spacers, thereby providing electrical isolation from the gate electrode;
    wherein each self-aligned contact further includes a conductive enhancement plug structured to reduce contact resistance to the at least one of the source or drain regions.

A synchronized dust-protective covering assembly for a sound membrane, including:
a housing configured to contain components thereof;
a sound membrane movably positioned within said housing, said sound membrane adapted to vibrate for producing or receiving sound waves;
a dust-protective cover movably arranged relative to said sound membrane and within said housing, said dust-protective cover designed to largely encompass said sound membrane when in a closed state, thereby impeding dust entry; and
a drive mechanism mechanically connecting said sound membrane and said dust-protective cover, wherein said drive mechanism is adapted to translate said dust-protective cover in close synchronicity with the reciprocal motion of said sound membrane, such that said dust-protective cover preserves a specified relative position or spacing concerning said sound membrane during use, thereby enabling sound propagation while preserving dust protection.

A method for lining a metal container, the method comprising:
