ascertaining a current operational state of the fuel cell system utilizing the at least one operational parameter, said current operational state being associated with one of a plurality of predefined operating modes;
choosing a particular voltage control stage from a plurality of distinct voltage control stages, each stage possessing a unique set of control parameters and a specific control algorithm, responsive to the determined current operating state;
producing a control signal derived from the chosen particular voltage control stage and the at least one operational parameter;
transmitting the control signal to a power converter connected to a fuel cell stack of the fuel cell system;
consequently regulating the output voltage of the fuel cell system in accordance with the chosen particular voltage control stage.

A method for electrochemically forming a three-dimensional structure, comprising:
