positioning a substrate within an electrolytic solution; and
imposing an electrical potential between the substrate and at least one counter electrode to selectively deposit or remove material from the substrate in accordance with the series of electrochemical fabrication instructions, thereby forming the three-dimensional structure.

A gaming device, comprising:
a processor arranged to conduct game play and produce a plurality of outcomes;
the processor further arranged to identify, from said plurality of outcomes, a subset meeting a predefined condition;
the processor further arranged to ascertain a quantity of the identified subset;
the processor further arranged to compare the ascertained quantity against a predefined award criterion;
and an output device coupled to the processor, the output device adapted to provide an award when the ascertained quantity satisfies the predefined award criterion.

A method for reconstructing a nuclear image, the method comprising:
acquiring raw nuclear imaging data reflecting radioactive emissions from a subject;
compensating the acquired nuclear imaging data for one or more of attenuation, scatter, or detector non-uniformity;
performing an iterative reconstruction of an image volume utilizing the compensated nuclear imaging data, wherein the iterative reconstruction involves employing a statistical model to adjust pixel values of the image across successive iterations until a defined convergence criterion is satisfied; and
producing a reconstructed nuclear image volume configured for display or further analysis.

1. An MRI apparatus, comprising:
a main magnet arranged to produce a static magnetic field within an examination region;
a gradient coil system adapted to create spatially varying magnetic fields within said examination region;
a radiofrequency (RF) coil system operative to transmit radiofrequency pulses into said examination region and to acquire magnetic resonance signals therefrom; and
a control system electronically coupled with the main magnet, the gradient coil system, and the RF coil system, said control system adapted to regulate the generation of the static magnetic field and the spatially varying magnetic fields, and the transmission of the radiofrequency pulses and acquisition of the magnetic resonance signals.

1. A method for regulating fragmentation of chemically strengthened glass, the method comprising:
