    chemically strengthening the glass substrate via an ion exchange process, thereby forming a compressive stress layer at a surface thereof; and
    adjusting at least one characteristic of the chemically strengthened glass article or a parameter of the ion exchange process;
    wherein said adjustment governs at least one fragmentation characteristic of the chemically strengthened glass article upon fracture.

A method for producing a photoelectric conversion device, comprising:
obtaining a substrate;
depositing a first electrode layer on the substrate;
forming a photoactive layer atop the first electrode layer, which is configured to absorb incident light and produce charge carriers;
forming a second electrode layer over the photoactive layer, such that the photoactive layer is positioned between the first electrode layer and the second electrode layer; and
structuring at least one of the first electrode layer, the photoactive layer, or the second electrode layer to delineate an active region of the photoelectric conversion device.

1. A disk drive unit comprising:
