    an optical scanning unit adapted to receive and deflect the light beam over a scanning area, thus creating a modulated light beam;
    a photosensitive member arranged to receive the modulated light beam and generate an electrostatic latent image upon it;
    a developing unit that applies toner to the electrostatic latent image on the photosensitive member to form a toner image;
    a transfer unit for transferring the toner image from the photosensitive member to a recording medium; and
    a fusing unit for fixing the toner image to the recording medium.

An MOS device, comprising:
a semiconductor substrate with a channel region;
a gate stack situated over the channel region, the gate stack comprising a gate dielectric layer over the semiconductor substrate and a gate electrode over the gate dielectric layer;
source and drain regions defined within the semiconductor substrate adjacent to the gate stack; and
a pair of dielectric corner spacers, each corner spacer positioned at a respective bottom corner of the gate electrode, wherein each dielectric corner spacer is located between the gate dielectric layer and a lower portion of a sidewall of the gate electrode, and wherein each dielectric corner spacer possesses a material composition distinct from the gate dielectric layer.

A printing system, comprising:
a processing unit adapted to obtain print job data, the print job data comprising content for printing and pertinent print parameters;
the processing unit additionally configured to evaluate the print job data and context information pertaining to a print request, wherein the context information encompasses at least one of user preferences, available printer resources, and network conditions;
the processing unit further arranged to formulate a modified print instruction set derived from the analysis of the print job data and the context information, the modified print instruction set improving printing performance or output quality; and
