confirming the speculatively identified prospective decompression operation; and
in response to a successful confirmation, employing the decompressed segment of the compressed data stream;
alternatively, if validation is unsuccessful, executing a non-speculative decompression of said segment of the compressed data stream.

A method for joint beamforming in a point-to-point wireless communication network, comprising:
transmitting a pilot signal from a transmitter having a transmit antenna array;
receiving the pilot signal at a receiver having a receive antenna array, and estimating channel state information (CSI) for a wireless channel connecting the transmitter and the receiver;
determining, at the receiver, a receive beamforming vector utilizing the estimated CSI;
generating, at the receiver, feedback information from the estimated CSI, the feedback information representing preferred transmit beamforming characteristics;
sending the feedback information from the receiver to the transmitter;
receiving, at the transmitter, the feedback information and calculating a transmit beamforming vector from the received feedback information;
applying, at the transmitter, the determined transmit beamforming vector to a data stream, thereby generating a transmit beamformed signal;
sending, from the transmitter, the transmit beamformed signal to the receiver;
obtaining, at the receiver, the transmit beamformed signal; and
utilizing, at the receiver, the determined receive beamforming vector on the received transmit beamformed signal to recover a data stream.

A transparent metallic millimeter-wave window comprising:
