wherein a second end of the first linkage element is configured to engage and pivot a second end of the second linkage element when the trigger is actuated, thereby causing the disengagement of the sear from the pre-stressed bowstring and imparting a mechanical advantage to the trigger pull.

A cardiopulmonary resuscitation device, comprising:
