1. A solid-state image sensor, comprising:
    a semiconductor substrate;
    a pixel array situated on the semiconductor substrate, said pixel array comprising a plurality of pixels, wherein each pixel includes a photodetector adapted to generate an electrical charge upon receiving incident light;
    readout circuitry disposed on the semiconductor substrate and operatively coupled to the pixel array, said readout circuitry configured to extract the electrical charge from each pixel and transform the electrical charge into an analog electrical signal;
    an analog-to-digital converter connected to the readout circuitry, said analog-to-digital converter configured to digitize the analog electrical signal into a digital electrical signal;
    control circuitry interconnected with the pixel array, the readout circuitry, and the analog-to-digital converter, said control circuitry configured to manage the operation of the pixel array, the readout circuitry, and the analog-to-digital converter, encompassing the timing of charge generation, signal acquisition, and conversion; and
    an output interface connected to the analog-to-digital converter, said output interface configured to transmit image data derived from the digital electrical signals.

A structural reinforcement system comprising:
