    a filter element positioned within the filtration chamber, the filter element configured for separating particulate matter from a fluid flowing through the filtration chamber;
    a fluid inlet formed in the housing and arranged to introduce unfiltered fluid into the filtration chamber;
    a fluid outlet formed in the housing and arranged to discharge filtered fluid from the filtration chamber; and
    an ejection mechanism functionally coupled to the housing and configured to selectively displace the filter element from the filtration chamber.

A method for gain measurement and monitoring within a wireless communication system, comprising:
receiving an input signal at an amplifier component within the wireless communication system;
obtaining a first characteristic of the input signal;
amplifying said input signal to generate an output signal;
obtaining a second characteristic of the output signal;
determining an operational gain value derived from the obtained first characteristic and the obtained second characteristic; and
monitoring said operational gain value by comparing said operational gain value against a predefined gain threshold.

A low profile spinal prosthesis comprising:
