    a charge transfer mechanism coupled to the plurality of photodetectors, said charge transfer mechanism configured to transfer the electrical charge from the photodetectors;
    a readout circuit coupled to the charge transfer mechanism, said readout circuit adapted to convert the transferred electrical charge into an output signal; and
    an output terminal coupled to the readout circuit, said output terminal configured to transmit the output signal.

An apparatus for the selective removal of stenotic material from a stent residing within a body lumen, comprising:
a flexible catheter body adapted for intravascular delivery to a stent positioned within a body lumen;
a treatment element positioned at a distal end of the flexible catheter body, the treatment element adapted to engage and remove stenotic material from the stent;
a sensing element situated at the distal end of the flexible catheter body, the sensing element adapted to discern a characteristic distinction between the stenotic material and the stent material;
a control unit operatively connected to the flexible catheter body, the control unit adapted to acquire data from the sensing element and to regulate operation of the treatment element based on the detected characteristic difference, thereby preferentially removing the stenotic material while substantially preserving the integrity of the stent; and
an energy delivery system operatively linked to the control unit and the treatment element, to furnish activation energy to the treatment element.

A writing instrument comprising:
