an output interface in communication with the processor, the output interface adapted to display details concerning the pinpointed one or more potential food-medicine interactions to the user.

A method for generating event messages based on event indicators, the method comprising:
obtaining, by a computing system, a plurality of event indicators, each signaling the occurrence of a particular event;
determining, for each obtained event indicator, an event type corresponding thereto;
retrieving event data from the obtained event indicator based on the determined event type;
choosing an event message template from a plurality of pre-established event message templates, wherein said choosing is based on the determined event type;
filling the chosen event message template with the retrieved event data, thereby creating a customized event message;
producing the customized event message;
and dispatching the customized event message to a specified recipient.

1. A handheld communication device, comprising:
