A method for mitigating thermal effects on a burden resistor within an electrical measurement circuit, the method including:
acquiring a raw voltage measurement across the burden resistor;
acquiring a temperature reading associated with the burden resistor;
retrieving stored temperature-resistance characteristic data specific to the burden resistor, wherein said stored data defines a correlation between the burden resistor's resistance and temperature;
computing a temperature-compensated resistance value for the burden resistor utilizing the acquired temperature measurement and the retrieved temperature-resistance characteristic data;
ascertaining a compensated current value flowing through the burden resistor employing the acquired raw voltage measurement and the computed temperature-compensated resistance value; and
providing the compensated current value.

A method for pseudowire protection, comprising:
