A method for low bias estimation of a signal-to-noise ratio (SNR) under low SNR conditions, the method comprising:
acquiring a composite signal that includes a signal component and a noise component;
obtaining a first statistical measure indicative of a total power of the composite signal;
obtaining a second statistical measure indicative of a noise power of the noise component;
utilizing an estimation function which combines the first statistical measure and the second statistical measure to yield an estimated signal-to-noise ratio, wherein the estimation function is specifically configured to minimize estimation bias that occurs when the signal-to-noise ratio is low; and
providing the estimated signal-to-noise ratio as a low-bias determination.

A marine propulsion system configured for efficient engine speed control, comprising:
at least one marine engine configured to produce rotational power;
at least one propeller functionally connected to the at least one marine engine;
a shaft system linking the at least one marine engine to the at least one propeller;
at least one engine speed sensor configured to ascertain an actual engine speed of the at least one marine engine;
at least one operational parameter sensor configured to measure at least one operational parameter reflecting a vessel operating condition; and
a propulsion control unit (PCU) communicatively linked with the at least one marine engine, the PCU adapted to:
    obtain the actual engine speed from the at least one engine speed sensor;
    obtain the at least one operational parameter from the at least one operational parameter sensor;
    determine a target engine speed utilizing the actual engine speed, the at least one operational parameter, and a predetermined efficiency metric;
    calculate a target engine speed delta, which represents a difference between the actual engine speed and the determined target engine speed; wherein adjusting the actual engine speed by said target engine speed delta guides the engine towards an optimal operating point in accordance with the efficiency criterion; and
    produce an engine control signal for adjusting the actual engine speed of the at least one marine engine based on the calculated target engine speed delta, thereby enabling efficient optimization of at least one of fuel consumption, power output, or emissions.

A method for reducing communication errors in a wireless communication system, comprising:
