A method for calibrating a downlink transmit path within a base station, said method comprising:
producing a test signal using a baseband processor of the base station;
transmitting the test signal via a downlink transmit chain within the base station;
routing a portion of the transmitted test signal from the downlink transmit chain into a receive chain within the base station;
down-converting and digitizing said routed portion of the transmitted test signal to yield a digitized feedback signal;
determining one or more performance characteristics of the downlink transmit path, based on the digitized feedback signal;
comparing the one or more determined performance characteristics with one or more desired performance characteristics;
computing one or more calibration parameters for the downlink transmit path responsive to the comparison; and
applying the one or more computed calibration parameters to modify operation of the downlink transmit path during subsequent downlink transmissions.

A method for deploying a complex computer environment comprising a plurality of interdependent software and/or hardware components, the method comprising:
