wherein the controller is arranged to receive input data from said one or more sensors and, responsive to said input data, produce control signals to selectively activate at least a subset of said multiple actuators, thereby inducing corresponding movement of at least a subset of said multiple pins to generate a dynamic tactile display or haptic feedback.

A system for registering a network access device amidst a power outage, comprising:
a network access device, including a communication interface arranged to send and receive data via a network;
a power management module adapted to monitor a primary power supply of the network access device;
a backup power source selectively actuatable to supply power to at least a segment of the network access device; and
a processor interfaced with the communication interface, the power management module, and the backup power source;
wherein the processor is operable to:
detect a diminution of the primary power supply through the power management module, signaling an imminent power interruption;
in response to detecting the diminution in the primary power supply, enable the backup power source;
commence a registration process with a network server through the network using the communication interface, which process is adapted to update a registration status of the network access device at the network server; and
send, utilizing power from the enabled backup power source, corresponding registration data to the network server before a total cessation of the primary power supply, thereby completing registration of the network access device amidst the power outage.

A system for the archival management of database logs, the system comprising:
a log acquisition module configured to acquire database log data produced by a database system;
an archival policy module configured to define one or more archival policies, wherein each archival policy sets forth criteria for identifying database log data suitable for archival;
a log archival module operatively coupled to the log acquisition module and the archival policy module, the log archival module configured to:
    assess the acquired database log data against the one or more archival policies;
    select database log data that meets the criteria specified by an archival policy;
    process the selected database log data for archival, wherein said processing encompasses at least one of compressing or encrypting said selected database log data; and
    generate archival metadata describing the selected database log data;
an archival storage module configured to retain the processed database log data and the generated archival metadata in an archival storage system; and
a retrieval module operatively coupled to the archival storage module, the retrieval module configured to accept a retrieval request for particular database log data and, by employing the generated archival metadata, retrieve the particular database log data from the archival storage system.

A wide area field emission display package, comprising:
