heating the polymer mixture to a temperature exceeding the melting point of the polyethylene resin to yield a molten polymer composition;
extruding the molten polymer composition through a die into a reduced pressure environment, thereby expanding said molten polymer composition and initiating the blowing agent to produce a foamed polyethylene material; and
cooling the foamed polyethylene material to stabilize its cellular structure.

