A device for tracking the position and movements of an eye, especially suited for ocular radiotherapy, comprising:
an image acquisition unit arranged to capture images of at least a portion of an eye;
an illumination source configured to illuminate said portion of the eye during image acquisition;
a processing unit communicatively coupled to the image acquisition unit and configured to receive said captured images;
wherein the processing unit is further configured to: examine the captured images to discern at least one anatomical landmark of the eye; ascertain a real-time three-dimensional position of the eye utilizing the discerned anatomical landmark; and monitor eye movements by continually updating said real-time three-dimensional position;
an output interface communicatively connected to the processing unit and configured to furnish data indicative of the tracked position and movements of the eye;
wherein the output interface is further configured to issue an alert signal or supply control data should the tracked position or movements depart from a predetermined tolerance range.

A data storage system comprising:
