at least one resilient element operatively arranged between the driver's compartment and the vehicle chassis;
and at least one damping element operatively disposed between the driver's compartment and the vehicle chassis.

A method for enhancing perceptual contrast in a subject, comprising:
    administering neural stimulation to one or more neural regions within a nervous system of the subject;
    wherein the administered neural stimulation is adapted to magnify a perceived difference between distinct stimuli or features encountered by the subject.

An apparatus for detecting lane delineation lines, comprising:
an image acquisition unit configured to obtain live image data depicting a roadway forward of a vehicle;
an image processing unit communicatively coupled to the image acquisition unit, said image processing unit configured to receive the live image data;
a feature extraction module integrated within the image processing unit, said feature extraction module configured to extract candidate line segments from the received image data;
a lane line classification module further integrated within the image processing unit, said lane line classification module configured to categorize and classify the extracted candidate line segments as lane delineation lines according to predefined criteria; and
an output unit linked to the image processing unit, said output unit configured to generate an output result indicating the classified lane delineation lines.

A medical image diagnosis apparatus, comprising:
a display unit configured to display a projection image of a subject;
a user input device configured to receive a user's selection of a designated point on the displayed projection image;
a processing unit coupled to the display unit and the user input device, said processing unit configured to ascertain a spatial coordinate associated with the selected designated point; and
a communication interface coupled to the processing unit, said communication interface configured to transmit control directives, derived from the ascertained spatial coordinate, to a three-dimensional (3D) imaging device, said directives instructing the 3D imaging device to capture a 3D image of a region of interest including the ascertained spatial coordinate.

A memory device, comprising:
an array of storage elements arranged in rows and columns, each storage element configured to store a data bit;
a plurality of word lines coupled to respective rows of the array of storage elements;
a plurality of bit lines coupled to respective columns of the array of storage elements; and
control circuitry coupled to the plurality of word lines and the plurality of bit lines, wherein said control circuitry is configured to select at least one storage element by activating a particular word line and a particular bit line, and to execute a memory operation on the selected at least one storage element, the memory operation comprising at least one of a write operation to store the data bit or a read operation to retrieve the data bit.

A texture processor, comprising:
an input interface adapted to receive texture-related input, wherein said texture-related input includes source texture data or parameters for texture generation;
a processing unit coupled to the input interface, said processing unit operative to perform at least one texture operation on the texture-related input, the at least one texture operation selected from the group consisting of texture synthesis, texture analysis, texture transformation, and texture filtering, wherein the texture operation alters or generates spatial patterns, surface properties, or visual characteristics of the texture;
a memory module coupled to the processing unit, said memory module adapted to store processed texture data; and
an output interface coupled to the processing unit, said output interface adapted to provide the processed texture data for a subsequent application.

A method for tunneling data link layer frames to facilitate high-speed data transfer in a noisy wireless environment, the method comprising:
  receiving, at a transmitting node, a data link layer frame;
  encapsulating the received data link layer frame into a tunnel frame by adding a tunnel header, the tunnel header containing error control information and sequencing information;
  applying an adaptive error resilience scheme to the tunnel frame prior to transmission, the adaptive error resilience scheme adaptively modifying at least one parameter based on observed wireless channel conditions to counteract noise effects;
  transmitting the tunnel frame over a wireless medium at a data rate optimized for high-speed throughput;
  receiving, at a receiving node, the tunnel frame from the wireless medium;
  processing the received tunnel frame, comprising performing error detection and, when necessary, error correction or requesting retransmission based on said error control information, said sequencing information, and said adaptive error resilience scheme; and
  decapsulating the original data link layer frame from the processed tunnel frame;
  wherein the encapsulation, adaptive error resilience scheme, and transmission collaborate to sustain high data throughput across the noisy wireless environment.

A method of coating a wafer for flip-chip applications, comprising:
furnishing a semiconductor wafer having a plurality of integrated circuits and a plurality of interconnection pads;
depositing a functional coating layer onto the semiconductor wafer;
structuring the functional coating layer to expose at least a portion of the plurality of interconnection pads;
and subsequently treating the structured functional coating layer to impart a desired property for subsequent flip chip assembly.

A communication method, comprising:
establishing a communication connection between a first and a second communication entity;
transferring data between the first and second communication entities over the established communication connection;
monitoring, by at least one of the first communication entity or the second communication entity, one or more dynamic conditions associated with the communication connection or the transferred data;
determining, based on the monitored one or more dynamic conditions, at least one optimized communication parameter for the data transfer; and
applying said at least one optimized communication parameter to the communication connection for subsequent data transfer.

An apparatus for forming a high dielectric film, comprising:
