one or more precursor delivery systems connected to the processing chamber, adapted to supply one or more film-forming precursors therein;
an energy source connected to the processing chamber, adapted to activate the one or more film-forming precursors to enable deposition of the high dielectric film on the substrate;
a vacuum system connected to the processing chamber, arranged to evacuate said processing chamber; and
a controller operatively coupled to the one or more precursor delivery systems, the energy source, and the vacuum system, adapted to regulate the film formation process to form the high dielectric film on the substrate.

A system for active database event management, the system comprising:
a database adapted to store data and issue one or more trigger events responsive to predefined database operations;
a trigger gateway including one or more processors and memory, the trigger gateway operatively linked to the database;
wherein the trigger gateway is configured to:
obtain the one or more trigger events issued by the database;
determine dynamically, using a set of externally defined trigger configuration rules, one or more trigger actions associated with an obtained trigger event; and
perform the identified one or more trigger actions outside of the database, thus offering a decoupled processing mechanism for database event triggers without integrating trigger logic directly into a database schema.

A rolling bearing comprising:
an inner ring;
an outer ring disposed concentrically with the inner ring;
a plurality of rolling elements positioned between the inner ring and the outer ring;
an integrated generator arranged to generate electrical energy from relative rotational movement between at least two components of the rolling bearing, the integrated generator comprising:
a plurality of magnets secured to a first component chosen from the inner ring, the outer ring, and a cage; and
a plurality of coils secured to a second component chosen from the inner ring, the outer ring, and the cage, said second component being distinct from the first component, such that relative rotation between the first component and the second component induces current in the coils;
a power management circuit electrically connected to the integrated generator, the power management circuit arranged to condition the generated electrical energy;
an energy storage unit electrically connected to the power management circuit for storing conditioned electrical energy; and
an output interface electrically connected to the power management circuit for supplying electrical energy to an external load, wherein said output interface is controlled by a control unit arranged to manage charging of the energy storage unit and discharge of electrical energy.

A method for forming a planarized layer of a semiconductor device, comprising:
