1. A downhole anti-rotation tool comprising:
a tubular body possessing a first end and a second end, the tubular body adapted for coupling with a wellbore tubular string;
at least one radially outwardly extendable anchoring member mounted on the tubular body;
an actuation mechanism operatively connected to the at least one anchoring member, the actuation mechanism arranged to selectively deploy the at least one anchoring member from a retracted state to an extended state;
wherein, in its extended state, the at least one anchoring member is adapted to contact an interior surface of a wellbore; and
