A method for operating a controlled system configured to generate a control output for influencing a process, the method comprising:
receiving an activation command for a control-hold mode;
responsive to the command, commencing the control-hold mode and recording a current control output value of the controlled system;
while in the control-hold mode, sustaining the recorded control output value as the control output for influencing the process, thereby preserving the process at a state corresponding to the recorded control output value, irrespective of subsequent changes in a control input signal; and
ending the control-hold mode upon receipt of a deactivation command or satisfaction of a predefined condition.

A method for producing a hollow structure for a breathing mask, comprising:
