a channel region interposed between the source and drain regions, said channel region comprising an elevated segment projecting upwardly from the semiconductor substrate;
a gate dielectric layer conformally situated atop at least the elevated segment of the channel region; and
a gate electrode disposed over the gate dielectric layer, wherein the gate electrode encompasses at least three sides of the elevated segment of the channel region.

A computer-implemented method for managing, observing, capturing, and reporting telephone access, the method comprising:
obtaining, by a computer system, a request for telephone access submitted by a user;
evaluating, by the computer system, whether to grant or deny the requested access in accordance with predefined access rules pertinent to the user;
regulating, by the computer system, such telephone access by either permitting or precluding said access pursuant to said evaluation;
observing, by the computer system, communication events linked to the telephone access, such as call initiation, call duration, and call termination;
logging, by the computer system, data related to each observed communication event, comprising user identification, timestamp, and communication event details; and
producing, by the computer system, a report from the logged data, said report presenting information regarding telephone access patterns and utilization.

A semiconductor integrated circuit, comprising:
a semiconductor substrate;
a plurality of active devices disposed on the semiconductor substrate;
a plurality of passive devices disposed on the semiconductor substrate; and
interconnection layers interconnecting the plurality of active devices and the plurality of passive devices to form at least one functional block, wherein said at least one functional block is configured to perform a predetermined operational method for the semiconductor integrated circuit.

A method for performance metric analysis of video assets, comprising:
acquiring digital video asset data representing one or more video assets;
gathering user interaction data associated with playback of the one or more video assets;
determining a plurality of performance metrics derived from the digital video asset data, the user interaction data, or combinations thereof;
evaluating the plurality of performance metrics to derive analytical insights regarding the performance of the one or more video assets; and
outputting an indication of said analytical insights.

I claim:

1.  A system for automated domain name registration, comprising:
    one or more processors;
    one or more non-transitory computer-readable media storing program instructions executable by the one or more processors;
    a network interface configured to facilitate communication with external domain name registries and domain registrars;
    a domain name request module configured to obtain a prospective domain name and associated registration parameters from a user;
    an availability checking module configured to automatically forward the prospective domain name to one or more domain name registries via the network interface and receive its availability status;
    a registration data generation module configured to automatically assemble registrant information based on the associated registration parameters;
    a registrar interface module configured to automatically dispatch the prospective domain name, the assembled registrant information, and a registration request to a selected domain registrar via the network interface following confirmation of its availability; and
    a payment processing module configured to automatically process and oversee payment for the domain name registration to the selected domain registrar.

A fluid-jet deposition method for radioactive material, comprising:
supplying a fluid containing a radioactive material;
forming a fluid jet from said fluid;
propelling the fluid jet onto a substrate;
whereby the radioactive material becomes deposited onto the substrate.

A system for enabling sequential lottery play, comprising:
a processor;
a memory coupled to the processor, the memory storing machine-readable instructions;
a communication interface coupled to the processor;
wherein the processor, when executing the instructions, is configured to perform operations including:
establishing a sequence of multiple lottery rounds, each round having a distinct set of lottery parameters;
receiving multiple player entries for a first lottery round of the sequence;
identifying winners for the first lottery round based on the multiple player entries and the distinct set of lottery parameters for the first lottery round;
orchestrating a transition from the first lottery round to a subsequent lottery round of the sequence, wherein the subsequent lottery round is influenced by an outcome of the first lottery round;
accepting player entries for the subsequent lottery round; and
identifying winners for the subsequent lottery round based on the player entries for the subsequent lottery round and the distinct set of lottery parameters for the subsequent lottery round.

An apparatus for managing and verifying algorithm modifications in a non-volatile memory, the apparatus comprising:
a non-volatile memory device adapted to store a plurality of algorithms, including updated algorithms;
a programmable processing unit operatively coupled to the non-volatile memory device;
an input interface operatively coupled to the programmable processing unit, configured to receive algorithm modification data including at least one algorithm or an alteration to an existing algorithm;
an output interface operatively coupled to the programmable processing unit, configured to output validation results;
the programmable processing unit further configured to:
store the received algorithm modification data in the non-volatile memory device;
run the modified algorithm from the non-volatile memory device with test data;
observe an operational output produced by the execution of the modified algorithm;
compare the observed operational output with an expected operational output corresponding to the test data;
ascertain a validation status based on the comparison; and
direct the output interface to output the validation status.

1. An apparatus comprising:
a prime mover engine;
a generator mechanically connected to the prime mover engine, said generator arranged to supply welding power for a welding process and supplemental electrical power;
an electric air compressor adapted to be powered by the auxiliary electrical power from the generator; and
